window.LUNA_CHAPTERS=(window.LUNA_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":51,"title":"Chapter 51 The Invitation She Couldn’t Accept","paragraphs":["Eira looked toward Alpha Killian’s office.","She knew exactly who had stalled her exit paperwork.","Before Miles could stop her, she walked in and closed the door.","\"Alpha Killian, I gave HR the thirty days’ notice required by my contract. I need my last day confirmed.\"","Alpha Killian looked up. \"What’s the rush? Planning to go back to Hale and play house?\"","\"No.\"","The answer came fast and sharp.","First Alpha Sebastian had tried to force her back into the role of a dutiful wife. Now Alpha Killian was trying to control when she could leave her job.","\"What I do next is none of your business,\" she said. \"My notice stands.\"","His brow furrowed at her distant tone.","\"You’re really set on leaving.\"","\"Yes.\"","\"And if I refuse to sign off?\"","\"You can hold up the paperwork, but you can’t reject my resignation. When the thirty days are up, I’m gone.\"","Her blue eyes held his.","\"If there’s nothing else, I’ll get back to work.\"","She turned toward the door.","\"Wait.\"","Alpha Killian pulled the RFP from his desk and dropped it in front of her.","\"The Sovereign Processor Initiative is active again. It started as Dr. Thorne’s project, and it’s in your field. Join Sterling Group’s proposal team.\"","Eira did not touch the folder.","\"I can’t.\"","She had seen confidential material from the original project. Advising one of the bidders now would create a serious conflict of interest.","He paused, then added, \"If you think the secretary position isn’t suitable, I’ll transfer you to the R&D center. Effective immediately.\"","A tech company’s R&D center held zero appeal for Eira.","\"No.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression tightened. \"You didn’t even think about it.\"","\"I didn’t need to.\"","\"You’d have your own team, a full research budget, and access to one of the best private labs on the West Coast.\"","\"Still no.\"","Alpha Killian leaned back, looking personally offended by how quickly she had dismissed the company he had built.","Then he tried one last angle.","\"Lila is joining our R&D division after she graduates.\"","Eira paused.","His expression eased. \"Interested now?\"","\"That’s great for Lila. Sterling Group will give her good experience. After a year or two, Professor Chase can help her move into a federal research lab.\"","Eira could also put in a good word for her, but Professor Chase’s recommendation would carry more weight in Lila’s field.","Silence filled the office.","She had just called Sterling Group a stepping stone.","Alpha Killian pointed toward the door.","\"Get out.\"","\"Of course, Alpha Sterling.\"","Eira left without hesitation and quietly closed the door behind her.","Alpha Killian stared at the closed door, his jaw tight.","--","When Alpha Sebastian received the invitation, he called an emergency meeting with Hale Group’s senior executives and lead engineers.","He had been following industry rumors for weeks and had already ordered his team to prepare a basic proposal. Now that preparation made him look brilliant.","By the end of the meeting, the project team was in place, the deadlines were clear, and Alpha Sebastian had put himself in charge.","His executives praised him for staying ahead of the curve.","Once the conference room emptied, Alpha Sebastian picked up his phone.","For some reason, he thought of Eira first.","Then he dismissed the idea. She would not understand how important this was. She would probably say That’s nice and ask what he wanted for dinner.","He called Serena instead.","\"Sebastian!\" Her excitement sounded instant and real. \"I knew Hale Group would make the list.\"","\"If we win this, it changes everything.\"","\"It’ll put Hale Group on the map. If you need anything from me, just ask.\"","\"I don’t want to put you in a bad position. You’re bound by your NDA.\"","\"Then I’ll stay out of the technical side.\" She paused. \"Have you told your family?\"","\"Not yet. You’re the first person I called.\"","The answer pleased her more than it should have.","\"Let me tell them. You have a proposal to finish.\"","Alpha Sebastian smiled. \"The deadline is tight.\"","\"I figured. Go make it count.\"","As soon as the call ended, Serena contacted the Hale family.","\"Hale Group has been invited to compete for a major contract,\" she told them. \"Sebastian is buried in work, so I offered to pass along the news.\"","Luna Margaret was thrilled. \"I knew he would get it. He’s worked harder than anyone for this.\"","\"I thought we could celebrate tonight,\" Serena said. \"Nothing too big. I’ll make a reservation.\"","\"That’s so thoughtful of you,\" Roger said.","Luna Margaret agreed at once. Serena was already acting like the perfect future Luna, handling family plans without Alpha Sebastian even having to ask.","Then Serena added casually, \"Should we invite Eira?\"","Luna Margaret’s mood cooled.","\"Why would we? She’s made it clear she wants nothing to do with this family.\"","Serena hid her smile.","\"I only thought it might be polite.\"","\"You’ve done enough. Let Eira sulk wherever she is.\"","The mate dissolution agreement had been signed and filed with the Pack Registry. Under Pack law, the marriage would officially end once the thirty-day waiting period expired.","As far as Luna Margaret was concerned, even that was too long.","She wanted Eira out of Alpha Sebastian’s life and Serena officially recognized as his Luna as soon as possible.","Serena booked a table at The Eden Garden, a new upscale restaurant, and shared the details in the Hale family group chat. Alpha Sebastian received a separate text telling him they were celebrating there that night.","--","Across town, Luna Seraphina had made plans at the same restaurant.","\"My beautiful, kind, incredibly generous mother,\" Lila began, \"shouldn’t you be taking Dad? If he finds out we went without him, he’ll complain about it for a month.\"","Luna Seraphina laughed. \"If I take your father somewhere this nice, I have to sit through a business dinner disguised as date night. I’d rather go with you and enjoy the food.\"","\"Smart choice.\"","\"Besides, the restaurant belongs to my friend Monica. It just opened, and I promised I’d stop by.\"","\"If we’re supporting a friend, can I bring one too?\"","Lila was already reaching for her phone.","Luna Seraphina glanced at the screen. \"Eira?\"","Lila looked up. \"How did you know?\"","\"You’ve mentioned her at least six times this week.\" Luna Seraphina smiled. \"And lately, she seems to be the only woman who can hold the attention of both Sterling siblings.\"","\"She’s easy to like.\" Lila pulled out her phone. \"Can we pick her up at Sterling Group?\"","\"Call her first,\" Luna Seraphina said. \"She may already have plans.\"","Lila sent Eira a quick text asking if she wanted to join them for dinner. Less than a minute later, her phone buzzed.","Lila grinned at the reply. \"She said yes.\""]},{"number":52,"title":"Chapter 52 The Unexpected Encounter","paragraphs":["Luna Seraphina watched her daughter’s face light up.","\"You really like her, don’t you?\"","\"Mom, you have no idea how incredible she is.\"","\"Because she found the problems in your thesis?\"","\"That’s part of it.\" Lila settled back in her seat. \"When Professor Chase saw my revisions, he couldn’t believe I’d fixed everything so quickly. He thought I’d need weeks, maybe even a whole new round of experiments.\"","\"But that isn’t why you admire her.\"","Lila shook her head.","\"Eira grew up in an Omega group home. She came to Palo Alto with no family money, no Pack connections, and no safety net. She built a life and a career on her own.\"","Her smile faded slightly.","\"And now she isn’t even working in her field because Alpha Killian hired her as his secretary.\"","\"Your brother didn’t force her to take the job.\"","\"No, but he’s certainly making it hard for her to leave.\"","Luna Seraphina raised an eyebrow. \"Is he?\"","\"I probably shouldn’t have said that.\"","\"Probably not.\"","Lila smiled, then looked out the window.","\"Everything I have came from you, Dad, and the Sterling Pack. I’ve worked hard, but I’ve never had to wonder whether I could afford school or where I would live. Eira never had that kind of support, and she still made something of herself.\"","\"That doesn’t make your own work less valuable,\" Luna Seraphina said.","\"I know. I just respect her. She’s brilliant, and she doesn’t need anyone’s approval.\"","Pride warmed Luna Seraphina’s expression.","\"You sound like a very good friend.\"","\"I’m trying.\" Lila’s grin returned. \"Honestly, I wouldn’t mind having her in the family someday.\"","Luna Seraphina laughed. \"Then your brother may need some help.\"","\"He needs a personality transplant. Most of the time, he says nothing. When he does speak, he sounds like he’s firing someone.\"","\"Some women appreciate a challenge.\"","\"Eira has suffered enough.\"","They were still laughing when the car pulled up outside Sterling Group.","Eira was waiting near the entrance. Her eyes widened when she saw Luna Seraphina in the car. Lila had forgotten to mention that her mother was joining them.","Lila lowered the window.","\"Surprise.\"","\"I noticed.\"","Luna Seraphina smiled. \"I hope you don’t mind me joining you.\"","\"Of course not. It’s good to see you, Seraphina.\"","\"Get in. We’re already late.\"","Lila moved over, and Eira climbed into the back seat beside her.","A security officer recognized the Sterling family car. Before it had even left the curb, word reached the executive floor.","Miles stepped into Alpha Killian’s office.","\"Your mother and Lila were just downstairs.\"","Alpha Killian looked up in surprise. His mother rarely came by without calling first.","\"Are they coming up?\"","\"Not exactly.\" Miles paused. \"They picked up Eira and left.\"","Alpha Killian had already started to rise.","He slowly sat back down.","--","The Eden Garden","The restaurant sat at the top of Riverside Tower. Greenery spilled from hanging planters, and the glass walls opened onto a view of the city. Soft violin music played in the background.","Eira’s olive coat fit right in with the garden setting.","Monica, the owner, came over to greet them.","\"Seraphina. Lila.\" Her gaze moved to Eira. \"And you must be new.\"","\"This is Eira,\" Luna Seraphina said. \"She’s a friend of Lila’s and works with Killian.\"","\"It’s nice to meet you, Monica.\"","\"You too.\" Monica smiled. \"I’ve heard good things.\"","She led them to a quiet table near one of the garden terraces.","\"I saved you the most private spot I could, but we’re still in our soft opening, so another party is seated nearby. The Hales booked a family dinner.\"","Eira’s shoulders tightened.","Lila noticed at once. \"Sebastian Hale?\"","Monica nodded. \"That’s the one. Five guests.\"","Lila counted them in her head.","\"His parents, his sister, and Alpha Sebastian make four.\"","\"The reservation was made by Serena Winthrop,\" Monica said. \"She listed herself as Luna Hale.\"","Eira picked up her water and took a slow drink.","Lila’s expression cooled.","\"That’s interesting.\"","Luna Seraphina glanced between them. \"Isn’t she the woman who came with Alpha Sebastian to the gala?\"","Before Lila could answer, the Hale family arrived and took the table behind them.","Isabella’s voice carried across the room almost at once.","\"Serena, how did you get a reservation here?\"","The Eden Garden was still in its soft-opening phase. It had no public booking system yet. Most tables went to investors, friends of the owner, and guests with the right connections.","Serena smiled. \"A friend from the research council got me on the list.\"","\"Of course she did,\" Isabella said. \"You know everyone.\"","She started to sit beside Serena, then changed her mind.","\"I’ll leave that seat for Sebastian.\"","\"Has he said how far away he is?\" Luna Margaret asked.","Serena checked her phone. \"He’s in the elevator.\"","Isabella grinned. \"He texted you and not the family chat?\"","\"Don’t start.\"","Serena’s blush only made Isabella smile wider.","A moment later, a host approached with Alpha Sebastian.","\"Your party is right this way, Alpha Hale.\"","Alpha Sebastian thanked him and loosened his tie as he crossed the dining room. He had expected a quiet dinner with Serena, not his entire family.","His steps slowed.","They were all there, smiling and ready to celebrate.","Everyone except his wife.","\"Sebastian.\" Serena raised a hand. \"Over here.\"","He started toward them, then caught sight of the woman seated at the next table.","Long golden waves fell down her back. A white dress showed beneath an olive cashmere coat, and a pearl gleamed at her ear when she turned her head.","Something about her felt familiar.","Monica glanced toward the Hale table.","\"Sebastian Hale keeps looking over here.\"","Eira’s back stiffened.","She had felt his eyes on her since he entered the restaurant, but she refused to turn around. Whatever he wanted, it could wait.","At the other table, Alpha Sebastian finally set down his coat.","\"That’s Luna Sterling,\" he told his family. \"I should go say hello.\"","Roger nodded. \"Of course.\"","Serena stood with him. \"I’ll come with you.\"","\"That’s not necessary.\"","\"I’d like to meet her.\"","Before he could object, Serena slipped her arm through his. Alpha Sebastian hesitated, then let her follow him.","They stopped beside Luna Seraphina’s table.","\"Luna Sterling, good evening. I don’t believe we’ve been formally introduced. I’m Sebastian Hale, Alpha of the...\"","His voice trailed off when he caught sight of the woman beside her.","\"Eira?\"","He pulled his arm free from Serena’s without thinking.","The sudden movement made Serena’s smile tighten.","Eira looked up at him.","\"What a coincidence.\"","Her tone was calm, almost bored.","No anger. No questions. Not even surprise.","The distance in her voice bothered Alpha Sebastian more than anger would have.","Serena recovered first.","\"Eira, I didn’t realize you had dinner plans here.\"","The words sounded friendly enough, but the question beneath them was clear.","How had Eira found her way into Luna Seraphina Sterling’s private dinner?"]},{"number":53,"title":"Chapter 53 Alpha Hale, You’re Hurting Her","paragraphs":["Eira lifted her chin.","\"I’m having dinner with friends.\"","Lila nodded. \"I invited her.\"","Alpha Sebastian and Serena exchanged a startled look. They knew Eira was close to Lila. They had not realized she was also comfortable around Luna Seraphina.","Alpha Sebastian’s gaze stayed on Eira.","Serena touched his sleeve.","\"Sebastian.\"","Then she turned to Luna Seraphina with a polished smile.","\"Luna Sterling, I’m Serena Winthrop. Dr. Victor Winthrop is my grandfather.\"","Luna Seraphina raised an eyebrow.","\"Then I’m confused. Your reservation asked the staff to call you Luna Hale.\"","Serena’s smile froze.","\"There must have been a mistake.\"","Monica spoke calmly. \"My staff used the title provided with the reservation.\"","Color rose in Serena’s cheeks.","\"I’m not Sebastian’s wife,\" she said quickly. Then she looked at Eira. \"She is.\"","Luna Seraphina turned to Eira in surprise. \"You’re married to Alpha Hale?\"","\"For the moment,\" Eira said.","Alpha Sebastian’s expression darkened. He caught her arm, but Eira pulled back.","Luna Seraphina’s voice cooled. \"Let her go, Alpha Hale.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked down and released Eira at once.","Serena frowned. \"Why didn’t you tell anyone?\"","Eira rubbed her arm. \"Sebastian spent four years keeping our marriage quiet. Ask him.\"","The answer wiped the last trace of satisfaction from Serena’s face.","Luna Seraphina looked between Alpha Sebastian and Serena, understanding settling over her features.","\"Eira doesn’t owe anyone an explanation,\" she said. \"She’s here as our guest.\"","Lila smiled. \"Exactly.\"","Luna Seraphina turned back to Alpha Sebastian. \"I believe your family is waiting.\"","The dismissal was polite but clear.","Alpha Sebastian kept his eyes on Eira. \"Meet me downstairs after dinner. We need to talk.\"","\"Okay.\" Eira’s voice was flat. Compliant.","Alpha Sebastian finally walked away with her.","Eira looked at Luna Seraphina. \"I’m sorry about that.\"","\"You have nothing to apologize for,\" Luna Seraphina said.","Lila picked up her menu. \"Good. Now can we order? Watching Alpha Sebastian get shut down made me hungry.\"","Eira laughed despite herself.","Luna Seraphina smiled, though questions remained in her eyes.","---","Back at the Hale table, Alpha Sebastian could barely follow the conversation.","Every few minutes, his gaze drifted toward Eira. He caught glimpses of her golden hair and the curve of her profile whenever she turned to speak to Luna Seraphina.","She was smiling.","That bothered him more than it should have.","Serena noticed every glance.","\"What happened over there?\" Isabella asked. \"And who was that woman you grabbed?\"","Serena forced a smile.","\"That was Eira,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","\"What?\" Isabella’s voice carried across the room.","A server appeared beside her. \"Ma’am, please keep your voice down.\"","Isabella flushed and waited until he left.","\"That was Eira?\" she whispered. \"What is she doing at dinner with Luna Sterling?\"","Luna Margaret glanced toward the other table.","\"She certainly moves fast.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression cooled. \"What is that supposed to mean?\"","\"She’s trying to trade up,\" Luna Margaret muttered.","Alpha Roger gave a dismissive shrug. \"One dinner with the Sterlings doesn’t make her one of them. Alpha Killian isn’t going to make a divorced Omega his Luna.\"","\"Divorced?\" Alpha Sebastian’s head snapped toward his parents. \"What are you talking about?\"","Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret exchanged a glance and shook their heads.","\"Nothing. Forget about Eira.\" Luna Margaret’s tone brightened artificially. \"We’re here to celebrate you.\"","She smiled at Serena.","\"And we have Serena to thank for putting all this together.\"","\"It was nothing,\" Serena said, pleased to have the attention back.","As dinner arrived, Alpha Roger leaned toward her.","\"This contract could change everything for Hale Group. If you hear anything useful, I hope you’ll point Sebastian in the right direction.\"","\"Dad,\" Alpha Sebastian warned.","Serena rested a hand beside her glass. \"I can help with public information, but I can’t discuss anything covered by my NDA.\"","\"We’re not asking for documents,\" Luna Margaret said. \"Even a small hint about what the review panel wants could help.\"","\"No,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"If Serena crosses that line, she could lose her position and face an investigation.\"","Alpha Roger sat back. \"Fine. Forget I asked.\"","Serena gave Alpha Sebastian a grateful smile.","\"Thank you for looking out for me.\"","She had ordered his usual steak, medium rare, with no sauce. It should have been exactly what he wanted.","Instead, it reminded him of Eira.","She used to know every small preference without asking. His coffee. His meals. Which tie he wore to Pack meetings. What he needed before he realized he needed it.","He had treated that care as if it came with the house.","Alpha Sebastian glanced toward her again.","Eira was laughing at something Lila had said. She looked more at ease with the Sterlings than she ever had at a Hale family dinner.","His steak suddenly had no flavor.","Alpha Sebastian pushed back his chair.","Serena caught his wrist. \"Where are you going?\"","\"To take care of the check.\"","At the host stand, he handed over his card.","\"Put both tables on this.\"","The hostess checked the reservations.","\"I can close out your table, Alpha Hale, but Luna Sterling’s party doesn’t have a bill.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. \"Why not?\"","\"They’re guests of Monica Vale, the owner. She’s dining with them.\"","Alpha Sebastian paused.","He was used to being treated with respect because of his title. The Sterlings moved through a different world, one built on old friendships and quiet influence.","What unsettled him was not that Eira had entered that world. It was how naturally she seemed to fit into it.","She used to be the woman who revolved around him. Now she had friends, plans, and an entire life he knew nothing about.","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","For the first time, he wondered how much of Eira he had never bothered to know."]},{"number":54,"title":"Chapter 54 You Reek","paragraphs":["As Eira and the others headed toward the exit, the Hale family arrived at the elevators behind them.","Luna Margaret’s face soured when she saw Eira.","\"You saw us earlier and couldn’t even come over to say hello? How rude.\"","Eira had expected this. Luna Margaret could turn anything into a reason to criticize her.","\"I didn’t want to interrupt your family dinner.\"","\"Your family?\" Alpha Sebastian’s voice sharpened. He did not like how easily she separated herself from the Hales. \"We’ll talk about this when we get home.\"","Eira looked at him but said nothing.","Alpha Sebastian could hardly explain the situation in front of everyone. Serena had planned the dinner and invited his family without telling him. Calling her out now would only embarrass her.","\"And show my parents some respect,\" he added. \"There’s no need for that attitude.\"","Before Eira could respond, Luna Margaret turned to Luna Seraphina with a tired sigh.","\"Please excuse her, Luna Sterling. Eira has never had much respect for family. At home, she can barely take care of her husband, much less the rest of us.\"","She wanted Luna Seraphina to understand that a nice dress and a few powerful friends did not change who Eira was. Once the marriage ended, Eira would never find another Alpha like Sebastian.","Luna Seraphina’s smile cooled.","\"I’m not sure why your son’s wife is expected to take care of you.\"","Luna Margaret stiffened.","\"In the Sterling family, we don’t expect a daughter-in-law to serve us,\" Luna Seraphina continued. \"We have staff when we need help. We also don’t expect her to wait on her husband. He’s an adult.\"","Luna Margaret’s face turned red.","\"I only meant that family should take care of each other.\"","\"Then the care should go both ways.\"","Luna Margaret had no answer.","Monica glanced at Alpha Sebastian. \"Alpha Hale, you might want to think about why you stood by while your parents criticized your wife. If you keep taking her for granted, you may lose her.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s hand tightened at his side.","He looked at Eira.","Lose her?","For four years, she had stayed with him even though he had given her almost nothing in return. She had never seriously threatened to leave. As far as he knew, nothing had changed.","\"Eira, I’ll wait for you downstairs.\"","He gave Luna Seraphina a polite nod, then followed his family into the elevator.","Once the doors closed, he turned to Serena.","\"Why didn’t you tell me you invited my parents and Isabella?\"","Serena blinked. \"I thought you’d be happy.\"","\"We were all sitting there like a family while Eira was left out. How do you think that looked?\"","He was still angry about the way Eira had called them your family, as if she had already decided she no longer belonged with them.","Serena’s eyes filled with tears.","\"I didn’t think about it that way.\"","\"Serena was trying to do something thoughtful,\" Alpha Roger said. \"Eira didn’t even bother to celebrate your success.\"","\"She didn’t know about it,\" Alpha Sebastian said sharply. \"If she had known, she would have planned something.\"","A tear slipped down Serena’s cheek.","\"It’s my fault. I should have included her.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression softened slightly, but his frustration remained. \"You should have told me who was coming.\"","The elevator reached the lobby, and Serena stepped out with her head down.","Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret motioned for Alpha Sebastian to follow her. Outside, Serena was already waving down a cab.","Alpha Sebastian watched her leave, but he did not move.","\"I’m waiting for Eira. I need to explain what happened tonight.\"","\"Explain what?\" Luna Margaret snapped. \"You don’t owe her an explanation.\"","When Serena opened the cab door, Luna Margaret gave Alpha Sebastian a push.","\"Go after her.\"","Alpha Sebastian turned to his mother.","\"No. And while we’re at it, stop criticizing Eira every chance you get. I’ve spent years focused on work while she handled everything at home. She took care of the house and made sure all of us had what we needed. She’s done enough.\"","Luna Margaret stared at him.","\"You hired a housekeeper. Don’t act like Eira did everything herself. And do you even know what she’s planning to do?\"","Alpha Roger shot her a warning look.","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes narrowed. \"What is she planning?\"","Luna Margaret quickly changed course.","\"She’s planning to make a fool of you. Look at how close she is to the Sterlings. How do you know she isn’t interested in Alpha Killian?\"","\"She wouldn’t do that.\"","No one knew better than Alpha Sebastian how much Eira loved him.","\"How can you be so sure?\" Luna Margaret demanded","\"Eira wouldn’t hide something like that from me.\"","Luna Margaret let out a bitter laugh.","\"Then what about Serena? She comes from a respected family, and she has stood by you for months. Are you really going to let people treat her like a homewrecker?\"","\"Mom, don’t say that about Serena,\" Isabella cut in. \"Sebastian and Serena were together first. Eira was the one who came between them.\"","The elevator doors opened behind them.","Eira stepped into the lobby with Luna Seraphina and Lila. They had heard every word.","Alpha Sebastian turned sharply.","\"Eira.\"","Isabella did not back down.","\"What? I’m not wrong. If Serena hadn’t gone abroad, Eira never would have had a chance. Serena should have been Sebastian’s wife from the beginning.\"","Eira looked at Luna Seraphina and Lila.","\"I’m sorry you had to hear this. You should head home. I need to deal with something.\"","\"You don’t have to stay,\" Luna Seraphina said.","\"I’ll be fine.\"","Luna Seraphina studied her for a moment, then nodded. \"Call Lila if you need anything.\"","\"I will.\"","Eira walked them to their car and waited until they drove away. Then she returned to the Hales.","She ignored Alpha Sebastian and looked directly at Isabella.","\"If you want Serena as your brother’s Luna that badly, convince your brother to divorce me. That would be more useful than yelling about it in a hotel lobby.\"","Alpha Sebastian stared at her.","Divorce?","No. Eira would never actually leave him.","\"You think I don’t want that?\" Isabella shot back. \"I think about it every day.\"","\"Enough,\" Alpha Sebastian said sharply.","He turned to Eira, and his voice softened.","\"I’m not divorcing you. Stop talking like that.\"","Then he looked at his parents.","\"Take Isabella home. Eira and I are leaving.\"","He reached for Eira’s hand, but she stepped away.","Alpha Sebastian told himself she was only upset about being left out of dinner.","\"It’s cold,\" he said, forcing himself to stay calm. \"Get in the car. I’ll explain everything.\"","\"I’m going back to Mrs. Thorne’s. I’m not going with you.\"","His jaw tightened.","\"Eira.\"","\"I said no.\"","Alpha Sebastian caught her wrist and pulled her toward the car.","\"Let go of me.\"","When she resisted, he lifted her into his arms.","\"Put me down!\"","He ignored her and carried her to the passenger side. He set her in the seat, then leaned across her to fasten the seat belt.","Eira pressed herself against the seat, putting as much distance between them as possible.","\"You reek.\"","Alpha Sebastian went still.","\"What did you say?\"","To Eira, his betrayal had tainted everything about him. Even having him this close made her skin crawl.","His hand closed around her chin.","\"What the hell is that supposed to mean?\"","A flash of panic cut through his anger.","Did she know about Serena? Was that why she had started acting so differently?","\"You just ate,\" Eira said coldly. \"You haven’t even brushed your teeth.\""]},{"number":55,"title":"Chapter 55 What Are Your Intentions Toward Eira?","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian remembered how particular Eira was about keeping things clean. She never left dishes in the sink or clothes on the floor.","But she had been gone for days, and the house was already a mess.","\"When are you coming home?\" he asked. \"The house needs you.\"","Eira gave him a flat look.","\"You can afford a housekeeper, Sebastian. It would cost less than a diamond necklace.\"","His expression changed.","\"What is that supposed to mean?\"","Eira caught the flash of guilt in his eyes.","\"Exactly what I said. Why? Does it mean something else to you?\"","\"Nothing.\"","\"Then why do you look nervous?\"","Alpha Sebastian looked away.","\"I’m not asking you to come back because I think you’re the maid,\" he said. \"I want you home because that’s where you belong. You can’t keep staying at someone else’s house.\"","His words reminded Eira of something.","She pulled out her phone and sent Martin a quick message.","[I’ve already had dinner, so please don’t have the kitchen prepare anything for me tonight.]","Alpha Sebastian noticed the phone at once.","\"When did you get that?\"","\"Recently.\"","\"What happened to your old one?\"","\"It barely worked. I should’ve replaced it months ago.\"","His unease grew.","Eira had new friends. She had changed the way she dressed. She no longer came home. Now she had a new phone he knew nothing about.","\"Why didn’t you tell me?\" he asked.","\"Do I need your permission to replace my phone?\"","\"That’s not what I meant. I could’ve bought you one.\"","\"No need. I can buy my own.\"","\"With what money?\"","Eira almost laughed.","\"Alpha Hale, I still take home four thousand dollars a month. It may not compare to your income, but it’s real money.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. He had never paid enough attention to know how much she earned.","\"Do you have to talk to me like that?\"","\"I answered your question.\"","He took a slow breath.","\"I didn’t know my whole family would be at dinner tonight. If I had known, I wouldn’t have left you out.\"","Eira looked up from her phone.","\"Then who did you think you were meeting?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s silence gave her the answer.","\"You thought it would be just you and Serena.\"","\"Hale Group is competing for a major federal contract,\" he said stiffly. \"Serena shared some public information and gave me general advice. Dinner was just a thank-you.\"","He watched Eira closely, waiting for her reaction.","She simply nodded.","\"Then why did you let her leave alone? That’s a strange way to thank someone.\"","\"I stayed because I told you I’d wait.\"","Surprise crossed Eira’s face.","Alpha Sebastian had let Serena leave upset so he could wait for her. That did not sound like him.","Unless he was feeling guilty.","\"If you’re driving me back, we should leave,\" Eira said. \"You may still have time to make things right with Miss Winthrop. What if she changes her mind about helping you?\"","\"She won’t.\"","\"You should be careful. I’m supposed to quit my job and stay home, remember? You promised me ten thousand dollars a month, plus the cost of my classes. If we have a baby later, that will cost even more.\"","Some of the tension left Alpha Sebastian’s shoulders.","She was still talking about quitting. About preparing for a baby. About a future with him.","So she knew nothing about Serena.","Eira noticed his relief, and a cold smile touched her lips.","He was easier to read than he thought.","\"I don’t need Serena’s help after this stage,\" Alpha Sebastian said as he moved into the driver’s seat. \"Anything more could put her career at risk.\"","He fastened his seat belt, then glanced at Eira.","\"Sterling Group received an invitation for the Sovereign Processor Initiative too, didn’t it?\"","Eira’s hand stilled.","\"Why are you asking?\"","\"You work directly for Alpha Killian. You must have heard something.\"","\"I know Sterling Group was invited to submit a proposal. That’s all.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s eyes sharpened.","\"Have you seen their bid?\"","\"No.\"","\"You’re leaving anyway. Could you look through the proposal before you go? I only need the main points.\"","Eira stared at him.","He was asking her to steal confidential information from Sterling Group.","\"I’m not on the proposal team, and I don’t have access to those files.\"","\"Alpha Killian keeps you close. You could probably get access if you tried.\"","\"No.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned at her quick refusal.","\"He made you his executive assistant right when you were planning to resign. He clearly trusts you.\"","The thought seemed to bother him more than it should have.","Then he leaned closer, his voice low.","\"I saw the way the Sterlings treated you tonight. Don’t let Alpha Killian fill your head with ideas.\"","Eira held his gaze.","\"What kind of ideas?\"","\"That you’d be better off without me.\"","The irony was almost laughable. A moment ago, he had asked her to betray her employer. Now he was warning her not to betray him.","Alpha Sebastian started the car.","\"Just remember who your husband is.\"","--","The Sterling Manor","When Luna Seraphina returned home, Alpha Julian was waiting by the door.","\"You went to Monica’s restaurant without me?\"","\"You would’ve spent the whole evening talking business.\"","Before he could argue, Luna Seraphina turned to Lila.","\"Tell your brother to come home. I need to speak with him.\"","\"Yes, Mom.\"","Lila escaped upstairs and immediately called Alpha Killian.","\"Mom wants you home tonight.\"","\"What does she want?\"","\"No idea. I’m just the messenger.\"","\"You had dinner with her. You must know something.\"","\"I know better than to get involved. Come home and find out for yourself.\"","She ended the call before he could ask anything else.","--","10:00 p.m.","Alpha Killian walked into the living room and found his parents waiting for him.","He sat across from them.","\"What’s this about?\"","Luna Seraphina did not waste time.","\"Do you have feelings for Eira?\"","\"No.\"","The answer came a second too late.","Alpha Julian gave him a knowing look. \"Try again.\"","Alpha Killian frowned. \"Nothing has happened between us.\"","\"That wasn’t the question,\" Luna Seraphina said. \"Did you know she’s married to Sebastian Hale?\"","Alpha Killian’s expression changed. \"She told you?\"","\"I found out at dinner. Alpha Sebastian grabbed her arm in front of us and called her his wife.\"","Alpha Julian’s face hardened.","\"You’re interested in a married woman?\"","\"I didn’t say that.\"","\"You didn’t have to.\"","Alpha Killian leaned back. \"What if she’s getting divorced?\"","Silence filled the room.","Luna Seraphina closed her eyes for a moment.","\"Killian, I’m going to ask you one more time. What exactly do you want from Eira?\""]},{"number":56,"title":"Chapter 56 Do You Have a Photo of Dr. Crawford?","paragraphs":["Alpha Killian did not answer right away.","Luna Seraphina studied him. \"That hesitation is exactly what worries me. You’re not sure what you feel yet.\"","\"I know enough.\"","\"Do you?\" Her voice was gentle but serious. \"You know what Eira has been through.\"","\"Yes. Her marriage to Sebastian is ending.\"","\"And you know how she grew up.\"","Alpha Killian’s jaw tightened. \"Growing up in an Omega group home doesn’t define her.\"","\"No, but it shaped her,\" Luna Seraphina said. \"She grew up without a family she could depend on. Then she trusted Sebastian, and he failed her.\"","Alpha Killian fell silent.","\"If you aren’t sure about your feelings, don’t rush into her life just because you want to protect her,\" Luna Seraphina continued. \"She doesn’t need to be rescued. She needs honesty, respect, and someone she can trust.\"","Her gaze held his.","\"So take the time to understand what you really want. If this is only anger at the way Sebastian treated her, let it go. If it’s more than that, be certain before you act. Don’t become another man who makes promises he can’t keep.\"","Alpha Killian looked down, considering her words.","Alpha Julian nodded. \"Your mother’s right. Don’t confuse wanting to protect someone with being ready to build a life with them.\"","After a moment, Alpha Killian met their eyes again.","\"I understand.\"","--","Winthrop Estate","The moment Serena entered the Winthrop estate, a housekeeper hurried forward to take her coat.","\"Miss Winthrop is home. Let Alpha Victor know.\"","Serena was the elder Alpha’s favorite granddaughter. Everyone in the main house knew it.","She greeted the staff as she crossed the hall, smiling and calling several of them by name.","\"Your grandfather is in his study,\" the housekeeper told her. \"He said you could go straight in.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Serena opened the study door without knocking.","Alpha Victor sat behind a large oak desk, reviewing reports from the Winthrop Pack’s research foundation. Several patrol maps were spread beside them. Even in his later years, his Alpha presence filled the room.","He looked at Serena over his glasses.","\"Ten days. I was starting to think your parents had locked you in their basement.\"","Serena smiled. \"They’ve been busy.\"","\"They’ve been busy for months, but I haven’t seen many results.\" Alpha Victor closed the report in front of him. \"What about you? The Sovereign Processor Initiative has entered the bidding phase. Where is the work you were supposed to publish?\"","Serena walked over and poured him a fresh cup of coffee.","\"Dr. Crawford hasn’t given me access to the approved research. I can’t publish anything or earn authorship if the core team keeps shutting me out.\"","Alpha Victor’s expression darkened.","\"You still haven’t been allowed into the lab?\"","\"No. I’ve been back for more than three weeks, and Dr. Crawford hasn’t even agreed to meet with me.\"","Serena sat across from him.","\"Everyone calls me Dr. Winthrop because they respect you. But no one asks for my opinion. The project team smiles at me and then leaves me out of every important meeting.\"","\"You were never promised access to classified data.\"","\"I know. I’m asking to join one of the approved research branches. I need work I can legally publish.\"","Alpha Victor tapped his fingers against the desk.","\"Professor Davies controls access now. Dr. Crawford makes the technical decisions.\"","\"That’s why I came to you. She isn’t only ignoring me. She’s ignoring your recommendation.\"","Alpha Victor’s expression hardened.","\"I’ll speak to Professor Davies.\"","\"I want to come.\"","\"No. I already used enough influence to get you onto the project. If we show up together, it will look like the Winthrop Pack is pressuring a federal research team.\"","Serena hid her frustration. She chose her words carefully.","\"Felix Shaw mistook someone for her at the gala. Has he ever met Dr. Crawford?\"","Alpha Victor gave a dry laugh.","\"His grandfather, Dr. Adrian Shaw, knew about her work. He and Dr. Thorne once competed to recruit her.\"","\"What about Felix? Has he ever met her?\"","Alpha Victor thought for a moment.","\" Dr. Crawford joined Thorne’s team seven years ago, while the work was still classified. After Thorne died, the program was suspended. It only restarted after she agreed to lead it.\"","\"So Felix wouldn’t recognize her?\"","\"He doesn’t have the clearance to access her identity records. If they met somewhere outside the project, I wouldn’t know.\"","It was not a complete denial, but Serena still felt some relief.","Alpha Victor studied her.","\"Why are you suddenly so interested in Felix Shaw? Did you see him at the gala?\"","\"Grandpa, you know I’m not interested in him. I already have someone.\"","\"Sebastian Hale.\"","Serena’s expression brightened. \"Yes.\"","Alpha Victor leaned back.","\"Hale Pack has grown quickly under him. Their territory has expanded, and their number of registered pack members has nearly tripled. He has also strengthened their patrol units and brought several smaller packs under Hale protection.\"","\"He’s a strong Alpha,\" Serena said. \"And while I was abroad, he invested heavily in my research.\"","\"Then focus on your own position before you worry about becoming his Luna.\"","The reminder stung, but Serena kept smiling. \"Can you tell me anything about Dr. Crawford? What she looks like? Where she’s from? If I could speak to her myself, I might be able to clear up this misunderstanding.\"","Alpha Victor shook his head.","\"Her identity is protected under federal security rules. Her photographs, address, Pack registration, and family history are sealed.\"","\"You don’t know what she looks like?\"","\"I’ve spoken to her through secure channels, but we’ve never met face-to-face. She avoids public appearances, and Professor Davies protects her privacy.\"","Serena’s heart sank.","\"So even you can’t help me reach her?\"","\"I can request a meeting. That’s all.\"","\"Dr. Thorne is gone. Professor Davies can protect her privacy, but he cannot shield her from every research council, contractor, and funding board.\"","His eyes turned cold.","\"No scientist works alone forever. Sooner or later, Dr. Crawford will need powerful allies.\"","\"We’ll remind her that the Winthrop Pack is better as a friend than an enemy.\"","That night, Eira received a text from Professor Davies.","Professor Davies: Victor Winthrop requested a meeting tomorrow at two. I need you there.","At the Winthrop estate, one of Alpha Victor’s staff quietly passed the same information to Serena."]},{"number":57,"title":"Chapter 57 The Photograph Sterling Group Headquarters","paragraphs":["The next morning, Eira arrived at work as usual.","Most of the executive floor was busy with Sterling Group’s proposal for the Sovereign Processor Initiative. Eira was not part of the bid team, so she spent the morning arranging Alpha Killian’s business trip.","It was her first time planning an executive trip. She reviewed his previous schedules, confirmed the flights and meetings, then built a tight itinerary around them.","Every hour had a purpose.","When she finished, she emailed the schedule to Alpha Killian and submitted a request to leave that afternoon.","Half an hour passed without a response.","Eira walked to his office and knocked.","Alpha Killian looked up from his computer. For a moment, he simply stared at her.","\"Come in.\"","\"Alpha Killian, I submitted a request for this afternoon. I need to leave by one.\"","\"Where are you going?\"","The question left his mouth before he could stop it.","Eira waited.","Alpha Killian remembered his mother’s warning and looked back at his screen.","\"Never mind. Log it as personal leave.\"","\"Thank you.\"","She turned to go.","Alpha Killian watched her leave, annoyed by how much effort it took not to ask again.","--","Shortly before lunch, Alpha Killian passed the break room and heard Eira speaking quietly on the phone.","\"Do you think Victor Winthrop is trying to pressure me because Dr. Thorne isn’t here anymore?\"","Alpha Killian slowed.","Eira listened for a moment.","\"I understand. I’ll be at the institute by two.\"","She ended the call and turned around. Alpha Killian stood a few feet away with a cup of coffee in his hand.","\"Alpha Killian.\"","She slipped her phone into her bag and headed for the door.","\"Wait.\"","Eira stopped.","\"If this meeting has anything to do with your work here, tell me,\" Alpha Killian said. \"Sterling’s legal team can handle any outside pressure.\"","Her eyes widened slightly.","\"You heard me?\"","\"Enough.\"","\"This is a personal matter.\"","Alpha Killian studied her face.","\"Then I won’t interfere. But if anyone tries to use Sterling Group against you, let me know.\"","Eira had expected questions. She had not expected him to respect the line she had drawn.","\"Thank you.\"","Alpha Killian nodded toward her bag. \"Your schedule for my trip is finished?\"","\"Yes. The itinerary and flight details are in your inbox.\"","\"Good.\"","He returned to his office and opened her email.","The schedule was clear, accurate, and painfully efficient. She had booked an overnight flight, followed by a breakfast meeting less than an hour after he landed.","There was no time to rest.","Alpha Killian stared at the screen.","She had arranged the trip as if sleep were optional.","Then again, he had delayed her resignation paperwork and made her handle a job she had never wanted.","Perhaps he had earned this schedule.","--","Silix Institute, 1:30 p.m.","Eira arrived at the institute half an hour before the meeting. The autumn wind cut through her coat as she crossed the entrance plaza.","She completed the retinal scan, stepped inside, and took a mask from her bag. After putting it on, she tied her hair into a low ponytail.","Professor Davies was waiting in the lobby.","\"This meeting is about Serena,\" he said as they walked toward his office. \"I’d bet money on it.\"","Ever since the gala, he had stopped calling her Dr. Winthrop outside formal meetings.","\"She already has a role in the project,\" Eira said. \"What else does she want?\"","\"Publication credit.\"","Eira frowned.","The Sovereign Processor Initiative was classified, but several related papers had been approved for public release. Serena had already been listed as a senior consultant despite her limited contribution.","\"She’s already ahead of half the team on the author list,\" Eira said. \"What does she want now? First authorship?\"","Professor Davies did not answer at once.","He could not rule it out.","\"She won’t get it,\" he said. \"Your name has already been submitted as first author. I made sure of that.\"","\"Good. If Victor tries to give Serena credit for my work, I’ll file a formal complaint and step down as technical lead.\"","Professor Davies glanced at her. \"You’d really leave?\"","\"I won’t let someone else claim research they didn’t do.\"","He could not argue with that.","When they entered his office, Professor Davies closed the door behind them.","\"There’s something else I’ve been meaning to ask,\" he said. \"Is your divorce final?\"","\"Not yet. The dissolution agreement has been signed. We’re waiting for the Pack Registry to issue the certificate.\"","\"At least Sebastian signed it.\"","Eira noticed the edge in his voice.","\"It’s fine.\"","\"No, it isn’t.\" Professor Davies frowned. \"You spent years cooking for him, managing the house, and taking care of his parents and sister. Meanwhile, he was flying overseas to see Serena.\"","Eira went still.","She knew Sebastian had sent Serena money every year. She had not known about the trips.","\"He went to see her?\"","Professor Davies’s expression changed. \"You didn’t know?\"","\"No.\"","He hesitated before answering.","\"More than once. I thought you knew.\"","Eira looked toward the window.","Of course Sebastian had never told her. While she stayed home and kept his life in order, he had been crossing the ocean to see another woman.","The money, the trips, and the years of silence had all been part of the same lie.","Professor Davies watched her carefully. \"Eira?\"","\"I’m fine.\"","Her voice was calm, but her eyes had turned cold.","A black sedan pulled through the institute’s main gate below. A few minutes later, Serena stepped out and headed toward the entrance.","Eira watched her cross the plaza.","\"It looks like Victor didn’t come alone.\"","Professor Davies joined her by the window and frowned.","\"I told him this meeting was limited to authorized participants.\"","\"Serena has temporary access to the administrative wing.\"","Eira turned away from the window.","\"Let her wait.\"","--","Victor arrived at the institute shortly before two and was taken to a conference room in the administrative wing.","A few minutes later, Serena entered using her temporary project badge. Her clearance allowed her into the administrative area, but not the secure labs.","At the security desk, she smiled at the guard.","\"Has Dr. Crawford arrived?\"","\"Good afternoon, Dr. Winthrop.\"","He checked her badge but did not answer the question.","Dr. Crawford’s schedule was protected.","Serena kept smiling. \"Of course. Security rules.\"","She walked away before he could ask why she wanted to know.","The administrative hall had a small seating area near the conference rooms. Serena chose a chair with a clear view of the corridor and pretended to read something on her phone.","Ten minutes later, three people appeared at the far end of the hall. Victor’s assistant led the way. Professor Davies followed, with a woman walking beside him.","Serena narrowed her eyes.","Professor Davies blocked most of the woman from view. All Serena could see were plain slacks, flat shoes, and a dark coat. Nothing stood out.","As they came closer, Serena quietly turned off her camera flash and sound.","Professor Davies reached for the conference room door.","Serena raised her phone.","Three quick photos.","The group disappeared inside without looking in her direction.","Serena immediately opened her photo gallery."]},{"number":58,"title":"Chapter 58 The Threat","paragraphs":["Professor Davies and Claire remained in the hall after Eira entered the conference room.","Victor’s assistant asked them to clear the doorway. Claire walked toward the waiting area, but Professor Davies only stepped a few feet back.","The assistant did not argue. She had other work to do.","Professor Davies remembered what Eira had told him.","Serena was in the building.","But why?","There was no project briefing today, and Serena had no access to the core research. She had no reason to be anywhere near this meeting.","Professor Davies scanned the hallway.","A flash of a designer skirt disappeared behind the corner. A pair of heels followed.","Almost everyone at Silix wore practical shoes and lab coats. Serena stood out wherever she went.","\"Dr. Winthrop?\"","Serena stiffened. She tried to slip her phone into her purse, but it fell from her hand.","It landed faceup on the floor.","A photograph filled the screen. It showed a masked woman walking beside Professor Davies.","Serena’s face went pale.","Phones were allowed in the administrative wing, but photography was strictly forbidden. Devices also had to be turned off near restricted meetings.","Professor Davies picked up the phone.","\"Professor, I came with my grandfather,\" Serena said quickly. \"I forgot to turn it off.\"","Professor Davies looked at the photograph.","Eira’s face was mostly hidden by her mask, but a few strands of golden hair had fallen across her cheek. Anyone familiar with her might recognize her.","\"I see,\" he said.","He opened Serena’s photo gallery and deleted the pictures. Then he cleared the trash folder.","\"There. The security issue has been handled.\"","Serena took the phone from him, forcing a smile.","\"Thank you, Professor.\"","Her relief lasted only a moment. Every photo was gone.","She tightened her grip on the phone.","\"That woman with you was Dr. Crawford, wasn’t she?\" Serena asked lightly. \"I’ve heard so much about her. I’d love to meet her.\"","\"It was Dr. Crawford.\"","Davies’s polite smile did not reach his eyes.","\"Her identity is protected for a reason. Photographing her inside a federal research facility could trigger a security investigation.\"","Serena’s stomach dropped.","If Professor Davies filed a report, both she and Victor would face questions. Her temporary clearance could also be revoked.","\"I understand,\" she said. \"It won’t happen again.\"","\"I hope not. I chose to delete the photographs instead of reporting you.\"","The warning was clear.","Serena adjusted the strap of her purse.","\"Of course. Please excuse me.\"","She turned and walked away.","Her original plan had been to wait until Dr. Crawford left the meeting and take a clearer picture. With Professor Davies guarding the door, that was no longer possible.","Serena glanced back once before entering the elevator.","She had come for Dr. Crawford’s identity.","She left with nothing.","--","Inside the Conference Room","Victor began with praise.","\"Dr. Crawford, this project would not be where it is today without you. Your work has been invaluable.\"","\"Thank you, Dr. Winthrop.\"","\"Of course, no project succeeds because of one person. Every researcher has played a part.\"","\"I agree.\"","Eira opened the file in front of her.","\"I can give you a full breakdown of each team member’s work.\"","She went through the list, explaining every researcher’s duties and results.","She did not mention Serena.","Victor’s expression tightened.","\"What about Serena? She’s been with the project for nearly a month. Surely she has brought something useful to the team.\"","\"Not quite a month,\" Eira said. \"So far, she hasn’t completed any technical work that qualifies for additional credit.\"","The answer was calm and factual. That made it harder to challenge.","\"Dr. Crawford, you remind me of your mentor.\"","Eira closed the file.","\"I’ll take that as a compliment.\"","\"You shouldn’t.\" Victor leaned back. \"Dr. Thorne was brilliant, but he made enemies everywhere he went.\"","\"If I achieve half of what he did, I’ll consider my career a success.\"","Victor’s patience slipped.","\"Dr. Thorne had the reputation and influence to survive those fights. You don’t.\"","\"I appreciate the advice.\"","Her polite tone only irritated him more.","\"Serena needs access to the core data,\" he said. \"Approve it.\"","Eira’s expression did not change.","\"She doesn’t have the required clearance or a technical reason to access it.\"","\"She’s a senior consultant.\"","\"Her title doesn’t override federal security rules.\"","\"I’m not asking you to give her control of the project. I’m asking you to let her review the data.\"","\"And I’m saying no.\"","Victor’s face darkened.","\"You’re one person, Dr. Crawford.\"","\"I’m the technical lead. Protecting that data is part of my job.\"","\"And if the review board approves her access?\"","\"Then I’ll file a formal objection. If they move forward anyway, I’ll step down as technical lead and withdraw any patent licenses under my control.\"","Victor stared at her.","\"Is that a threat?\"","\"It’s the consequence of giving classified research to someone who hasn’t worked on it and doesn’t need it.\"","\"You’re doing this because you dislike Serena.\"","\"No. You placed Serena on my team without consulting me. I accepted the decision. What I won’t accept is giving her access she hasn’t earned.\"","Victor’s face flushed with anger.","Eira watched him for a moment.","\"Do you need a minute?\"","\"Get out.\"","She stood and gathered her files.","\"Dr. Crawford.\"","Eira paused at the door.","Victor’s voice turned cold.","\"You’re talented, but talent only takes you so far. Research depends on funding, partnerships, and reputation. Keep making enemies, and you may find that no one wants to work with you after this project.\"","Eira met his eyes.","\"Is that professional advice, or are you threatening to interfere with my career?\"","Silence followed.","Victor had no answer he could safely give.","Eira opened the door.","\"I’ll make a note of this conversation.\"","Then she walked out.","Professor Davies was waiting in the hall. The moment he saw her, he held out her mask.","\"Put this back on.\"","Eira noticed the tension in his face and covered her nose and mouth.","\"What happened?\"","\"Serena was hiding in the administrative wing and taking pictures of you.\"","Eira stopped.","\"Did she see my face?\"","\"I don’t think so. I deleted the photos and cleared the trash folder.\"","\"You should’ve reported her.\"","\"I still might.\" Professor Davies glanced toward the nearby security camera. \"The hallway footage will show what she did.\"","Eira adjusted her mask.","\"Then file the report. If we ignore it, she’ll try again.\"","Professor Davies nodded. \"I’ll speak to security.\"","His voice dropped.","\"Until this is handled, use a different entrance and change your coat before you leave. Serena is already looking for a connection between you and Dr. Crawford.\"","\"And if she tells Sebastian?\"","\"That’s what worries me. If they compare what they know, they may figure it out.\"","Eira thought of Sebastian asking her to find Sterling Group’s bid documents.","\"He already tried to get confidential information from me.\"","Professor Davies’s expression hardened. \"Then we assume both of them are a security risk.\"","He handed her a written security notice.","\"Your identity protects more than your privacy. It protects access to the project. Don’t let anyone use your badge, devices, or biometric records.\""]},{"number":59,"title":"Chapter 59 The Missing Package","paragraphs":["Serena had not left the institute yet. As long as she remained in the building, she might catch another glimpse of Eira.","Professor Davies took off his black blazer and handed it to her.","\"Put this on.\"","It was too large, but it covered most of her clothes.","He pulled a worn gray baseball cap from his bag. \"And this.\"","Eira put it on and lowered the brim.","\"Why do you have a baseball cap?\"","\"It belongs to my daughter.\" Professor Davies checked her disguise. \"From now on, bring a change of clothes when you come here. We can’t be too careful.\"","\"Understood.\"","Professor Davies led her to the underground garage and drove toward the exit. As they reached the security gate, he spotted Serena in the rearview mirror. She was standing near the lobby doors, watching every car that passed.","Professor Davies muttered under his breath.","\"She’s still here. I’ll have to speak to Victor. He may be the only person who can stop her.\"","Once they were outside the institute, he glanced at Eira.","\"Where should I take you?\"","Eira was about to say the Thorne estate when her phone buzzed.","It was Miss Gwen, the director of the Omega children’s home where she had grown up.","Professor Davies motioned for her to answer.","\"Hi, Miss Gwen.\"","Eira’s expression softened at once.","\"I’m doing well. How are you? How are the kids?\"","\"We’re all doing great, sweetheart. The children made some things for you. Letters, drawings, and little crafts. We also sent treats from home. Your favorite spicy peanut brittle is in there.\"","Eira smiled.","\"The tracking says the package was delivered to your place,\" Miss Gwen continued. \"Don’t forget to pick it up.\"","\"I’ll get it today.\"","Eira had always used the apartment she shared with Alpha Sebastian as her mailing address. She would need to change that soon.","\"Miss Gwen, please don’t send anything else to that address. I’m going to be moving.\"","\"Oh, are you and Alpha Sebastian moving?\"","Miss Gwen sounded pleased. Eira could not bring herself to tell her about the divorce over the phone.","\"Yes. I’ll send you my new address once I’m settled.\"","\"All right. You’re still coming to visit after New Year’s, aren’t you? The kids are counting down the days. They keep saying, ’First fall, then winter, and then Miss Eira comes home.’\"","Eira’s smile reached her eyes.","\"I’ll be there. Sebastian won’t be able to come this time, though. He’s been busy with work.\"","\"That’s all right. As long as you come, the children will be happy.\"","\"I wouldn’t miss it.\"","\"And don’t forget to share the treats. Some of them won’t keep for long. Give some to Alpha Sebastian, his parents and sister, and your professors and friends. We packed plenty.\"","Emotion tightened Eira’s throat.","\"You tell me that every time.\"","\"Are you tired of hearing it?\" Miss Gwen teased.","\"Never. I’ll never get tired of it.\"","Miss Gwen laughed, though her voice wavered slightly.","\"All right, sweetheart. I’ll let you go. Make sure you eat something tonight.\"","\"I will.\"","After the call ended, Professor Davies glanced at her.","\"You haven’t told her about the divorce?\"","\"I don’t know how,\" Eira admitted. \"Sebastian came with me every year. He donated money and brought gifts for every child. They all adore him.\"","That was what made the memories so difficult to understand.","Alpha Sebastian had shown patience and kindness to the children. He could be generous to strangers and loyal to Serena. Yet somehow, he had never given Eira enough honesty to make their marriage real.","She looked out the window.","\"Professor Davies, could you take me to the Hale apartment? I need to pick up the package from Miss Gwen and the kids.\"","Professor Davies nodded and changed lanes.","\"Of course.\"","The car stopped outside the house Eira shared with Alpha Sebastian.","Eira opened the door. \"Thanks for the ride, Professor. I won’t invite you in today, but once things settle down, I’ll cook you a proper dinner.\"","Professor Davies brightened. Eira sometimes brought extra food to the institute, and he had never turned it down.","\"I’ll hold you to that. And I’ll help with the cooking.\"","Eira smiled and watched his car disappear down the street.","She had not been home in days.","The house felt cold when she stepped inside. Takeout containers sat on the kitchen counter, and several unopened packages had been left by the front door.","All of them were from the children’s home.","Eira found a box cutter and opened the packages one by one. They were filled with snacks, dried food, and local treats.","But there were no letters, drawings, or handmade gifts from the children.","She checked every box again.","Nothing.","Eira called Miss Gwen.","\"What kind of box did you put the children’s gifts in?\"","\"A square cardboard box,\" Miss Gwen said. \"Why? Isn’t it there?\"","\"I can’t find it. I’ll check with the delivery company.\"","The driver confirmed that every package had been delivered. The photo he sent clearly showed a square box sitting with the others by the front door.","Someone had taken it.","Only that box was missing.","Eira stood among the open packages and called Alpha Sebastian.","\"Did you come home today? One of the boxes from Miss Gwen is gone.\"","\"You’re home?\" Hope entered his voice at once.","\"Answer the question, Sebastian. Did you open any of the packages?\"","\"No. I haven’t been there today.\" He paused. \"But Isabella stopped by.\"","Eira looked at the empty space beside the other packages.","Her stomach sank.","Isabella had taken the box","Alpha Sebastian started to say something else, but Eira cut him off.","\"I’ll call you back. I need to speak to Isabella.\"","\"Don’t worry. The box is probably somewhere in the house. Isabella wouldn’t touch your things.\"","Eira closed her eyes.","Alpha Sebastian had defended his sister with the same excuse for years. Eira had tried to tell him what Isabella was really like, but he had never listened.","She was done trying. Eira ended the call."]},{"number":60,"title":"Chapter 60 Eira Snaps","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian stared at his phone.","She had hung up on him.","When had she started doing that?","He grabbed his coat and left the office. On his way to the elevator, he sent Eira a list of what he wanted for dinner.","After several days of takeout and office catering, he was looking forward to a proper meal at home.","Eira did not read the message. She called Isabella instead.","The first call was declined.","So was the second.","Isabella finally answered on the third try.","\"Wow. Luna Eira called me first. Should I feel honored?\"","\"You took one of my packages.\"","\"So what if I did?\"","Isabella did not even try to deny it.","\"That children’s home sends you boxes of cheap junk every year, and then you pass the stuff around like we’re supposed to be grateful. We don’t want it.\"","Eira’s grip tightened around the phone. \"Where is the box?\"","\"With me.\"","\"Then bring it back.\"","Isabella laughed. \"Why? So you can hand out stale snacks and ugly little crafts again?\"","A cold feeling settled in Eira’s chest. \"What do you mean, again?\"","Isabella went quiet for a second. Then she gave a careless sigh.","\"Come on, Eira. Did you really think we kept all that stuff every year? Most of it went straight into the trash before Sebastian saw it.\"","Eira stopped breathing. \"The letters too?\"","\"What else were we supposed to do with them?\"","\"You could have given them back to me. \"Her voice remained steady, but it took everything she had to keep it that way.","Years of letters. Drawings made by small hands. Gifts the children had spent hours making for her.","All gone.","\"Return the box you took today,\" Eira said.","\"You want it?\" Isabella’s voice turned playful. \"Come get it yourself.\"","\"Where are you?\"","\"I’m busy. I’ll tell you when I have time.\"","\"Isabella.\"","\"And don’t complain to Sebastian. If you do, I’ll tear up every letter and drawing in the box.\"","So she had already opened it.","Eira forced herself to breathe slowly. \"What do you want?\"","\"I want you out of my brother’s life.\"","\"Then talk to Sebastian. He’s the one refusing to let go.\"","Isabella scoffed. \"He obviously loves Serena. I don’t understand why he won’t divorce you.\"","\"Neither do I.\"","\"Maybe because you keep making him feel sorry for you.\"","Eira ignored the insult. \"You took a package addressed to me. Return it today.\"","\"Or what?\"","\"Or I report it stolen.\"","Isabella gave a short laugh, but a hint of unease entered her voice. \"You wouldn’t call the police over a box of trash.\"","\"It isn’t trash. It belongs to me.\"","\"You’re seriously threatening me?\"","\"No. I’m telling you what happens next.\"","Isabella fell silent. Then her anger returned.","\"I don’t have time for this. You’ll get it back when I decide you can have it.\"","Isabella ended the call.","Eira immediately sent Isabella a text.","[Don’t touch anything in that box. If even one letter is damaged, I’ll freeze your study-abroad fund.]","Isabella’s reply came almost at once.","[WHY DON’T YOU JUST DROP DEAD, EIRA?]","Another message followed.","[I KNEW YOU WERE CONTROLLING MY BROTHER’S MONEY. YOU’VE BEEN TRYING TO RUIN MY LIFE THIS WHOLE TIME!]","Then came a third.","[I’m not touching that disgusting box anyway. Who knows what kind of germs are on it?]","Eira gave a cold smile.","Isabella could believe whatever she wanted. The only thing that mattered was keeping the children’s gifts safe.","Eira looked at the open packages around the entryway. She could not leave them there, and she certainly could not take them back to the Thorne estate.","She decided to move everything to the small house she owned. It had been empty for some time, but at least no one in the Hale family could touch her things there.","Eira packed the food and gifts into several large bags. She planned to take a cab, but she had barely dragged everything into the hall when the elevator doors opened.","Alpha Sebastian stepped out.","They passed each other near the doorway.","Eira was still wearing Professor Davies’s oversized black blazer. A baseball cap covered most of her hair, and a mask hid the lower half of her face.","Alpha Sebastian walked past without recognizing her.","Then he stopped.","Something about the woman in the hall felt familiar.","\"Eira?\"","She paused. That brief hesitation gave her away.","Alpha Sebastian turned and walked back toward her. He pulled off her cap before she could stop him, then reached for her mask.","Eira stepped back and removed it herself.","\"What are you wearing?\" His gaze settled on the oversized blazer. \"Whose is that?\"","\"A colleague’s.\"","\"What colleague?\"","\"A professor you don’t know.\"","Alpha Sebastian studied her face, but her expression gave him nothing.","Then he noticed the bags in her hands. The handles had left red marks across her palms.","\"You’ve been gone for days. Did all this pile up while you were away?\"","Eira’s eyes cooled.","Isabella had called the packages disgusting. Now Alpha Sebastian was treating them like clutter.","She adjusted her grip and walked past him.","Alpha Sebastian reached for one of the bags.","\"I’ll take them to the trash room. Did you buy groceries? What are you making for dinner?\"","Eira moved the bag out of his reach.","\"These aren’t trash. They’re care packages from Miss Gwen and the children.\"","Alpha Sebastian paused.","\"And I’m keeping them this year,\" she continued. \"That way, your family won’t have to throw them out behind my back.\"","His expression changed. \"What are you talking about?\"","\"Isabella admitted it. She said your family has been throwing away the packages for years. The food, the letters, and the children’s drawings.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. \"I knew my parents didn’t like some of the food, but I didn’t know they threw away the children’s things.\"","\"Of course you didn’t.\"","Her answer was quiet, but the bitterness in it was clear.","Eira picked up the last bag.","\"I’m leaving.\"","\"You just got here.\" Alpha Sebastian caught her arm. \"Where are you going?\"","\"That’s none of your business.\"","\"I left work early so we could have dinner. Are you seriously leaving again?\"","\"I never asked you to come home.\"","His face hardened. \"Do you care about this home at all?\"","Eira turned to him. \"I should be asking you that.\"","\"If I didn’t care, why would I leave work and come straight here?\"","\"Because you’re tired of takeout.\"","Alpha Sebastian stared at her.","Eira’s voice remained calm. \"You missed having someone cook for you, clean up after you, and keep the house running. That isn’t the same as missing me.\"","\"That’s not true.\"","\"Isn’t it?\" Her eyes held his.","\"You got bored with what you had at home, so you went looking for something more exciting. Now you want to come back because home is familiar and convenient.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened. \"You’re reading too much into this. I like your cooking. I’m used to it.\"","Eira let out a short, bitter laugh.","Used to it.","That explained everything.","Her food suited him. Her silence suited him. Her willingness to manage his life suited him.","He did not love her. He simply liked the role she filled.","\"And I haven’t been avoiding this place,\" Alpha Sebastian added. \"You’re the one who disappeared. Do you even know how many days you’ve been gone?\"","\"How many?\"","He opened his mouth, then stopped.","\"I’ve been busy. I don’t keep track of every day.\"","\"Exactly.\" Eira pulled her arm free and reached for the bags.","Alpha Sebastian blocked her path. \"You’re not leaving tonight.\"","\"You have a husband and a home. You can’t keep walking away whenever you’re upset.\""]},{"number":61,"title":"Chapter 61 The Market","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian blocked the door.","\"We’re having dinner together tonight.\"","Eira glanced at his hand around her wrist. Arguing would only waste more time.","\"Fine. I’ll cook. Now let go.\"","He released her.","\"The fridge is empty, so I need groceries.\" She pointed to the care packages. \"Put those inside first.\"","\"I’m coming with you.\"","Eira looked at him. \"You haven’t gone grocery shopping once in four years.\"","\"There’s a first time for everything.\"","They carried the packages inside, then walked to the neighborhood market.","It was busy with people stopping in after work. The narrow aisles were lined with fresh produce, baked bread, and small meat and seafood counters.","Alpha Sebastian stood out in his suit and polished shoes.","He nearly stepped into a wet patch by the produce section and frowned.","\"Why don’t you order groceries online?\"","\"Because the delivery fees add up, and this place has better produce.\"","Eira picked up a bunch of green onions, checked them, and placed them in her basket.","Alpha Sebastian looked at the price tag. \"You don’t have to worry about saving a few dollars.\"","Eira turned to him.","\"You give me three thousand dollars a month to run the house.\"","\"That should be enough.\"","\"It covers groceries, toiletries, cleaning supplies, small repairs, and every dinner your parents expect me to host. It also covers the extra food Isabella takes home whenever she visits.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s frown deepened.","\"You could’ve told me you needed more.\"","\"I did.\"","He went quiet.","\"More than once,\" Eira added.","She moved on before he could defend himself.","Alpha Sebastian followed as she checked weekly specials and compared prices. He had never thought about how much work went into keeping the house stocked. Food appeared in the kitchen. Soap appeared in the bathrooms. His parents came over for dinner, and everything was ready.","He had never asked how.","At the seafood counter, Mr. Caldwell smiled when he saw Eira.","\"Well, look who finally showed up.\"","Eira managed a small smile. \"Hi, Mr. Caldwell.\"","\"Haven’t seen you in a while. I was starting to think you’d found a better fish guy.\"","\"Never. I’ve just been busy.\"","\"That’s what they all say.\"","He pulled on a pair of gloves and lifted a fresh fish from the display.","\"I saved one for you last week, but you never came in.\"","\"You don’t need to do that anymore.\" Eira paused. \"I’m moving.\"","Mr. Caldwell looked up.","\"You’re leaving the neighborhood?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Well, that’s a shame. You’re one of the few customers who actually knows what she’s buying.\"","\"Thank you for always looking out for me.\"","\"Anytime.\"","As he wrapped the fish, he noticed Alpha Sebastian approaching behind her.","\"Your husband?\" he asked casually.","Eira did not hesitate.","\"No.\"","Alpha Sebastian heard her. His steps slowed.","Mr. Caldwell glanced between them, clearly sensing that he had walked into something complicated.","\"What did he ask you?\" Alpha Sebastian said.","\"Nothing important.\"","\"I heard you say no.\"","\"Then you already heard the answer.\"","Mr. Caldwell wisely handed the fish to Alpha Sebastian and turned to the next customer.","Eira’s phone rang as they headed toward the meat counter.","\"I need to take this.\"","She stepped aside.","It was Lila.","\"Please tell me you’re free for dinner,\" Lila said.","Eira glanced at the groceries in Alpha Sebastian’s hands.","\"Actually, Lila, would you like to come over? I can cook dinner.\"","\"Are you serious?\" Lila sounded delighted. \"Send me the address. I’m on my way.\"","\"I need a favor too.\"","\"Name it.\"","\"You don’t even know what I’m asking.\"","\"Unless you need me to hide a body, I’m probably in.\"","Warmth spread through Eira’s chest.","\"I’ll explain when you get here.\"","Alpha Sebastian walked over when he saw her smile.","\"Who are you talking to?\"","\"A friend.\"","Eira made no effort to hide the screen. Alpha Sebastian saw Lila Sterling’s name and immediately thought of Alpha Killian.","Eira ended the call and looked at him.","\"I invited Lila to dinner. Is that a problem?\"","Alpha Sebastian hesitated. Eira had never brought a friend home before.","\"Fine.\"","\"You can invite someone too.\"","She meant Serena, and they both knew it.","Alpha Sebastian took out his phone and texted Ethan Yates instead.","\"Ethan’s coming.\"","\"What about Miss Winthrop?\"","Tension crossed his face.","\"Why would I invite her?\"","\"She’s your friend. Ethan knows her too.\"","\"Not tonight,\" Alpha Sebastian said quickly. \"Let’s go.\"","\"I need a few more things. It’s Lila’s first time trying my cooking.\"","The warmth in Eira’s voice made Alpha Sebastian frown.","\"You seem pretty eager to impress her.\"","\"She’s my friend.\"","\"Since when?\"","\"Since she treated me like one.\"","The answer hit harder than he expected.","Alpha Sebastian followed as Eira added a few more items to the cart.","\"What do you two even have in common?\"","\"More than you think.\"","He wanted to ask what that meant, but Eira had already turned back to the produce.","Her whole mood had changed. A few minutes ago, she had barely looked at him. Now she was planning dinner for Lila with a small smile on her face.","Alpha Sebastian could not remember when Eira had stopped smiling like that around him.","After picking up the last few ingredients, Eira sent Lila a text.","[I need you to get me out of the apartment tonight. No matter what happens, I can’t stay here with Sebastian.]","Lila replied almost at once.","[Consider it done.","Eira put away her phone and turned to Alpha Sebastian.","\"Let’s go.\""]},{"number":62,"title":"Chapter 62 Ungrateful","paragraphs":["As soon as they returned to the apartment, Eira carried the groceries into the kitchen and started dinner.","She had chosen every pot, dish, and tool with Alpha Sebastian’s tastes in mind. He had never noticed.","To him, the kitchen had simply appeared one day, complete and ready to use.","Alpha Sebastian settled onto the couch and turned on the evening news. Every few minutes, he glanced through the open kitchen doorway.","Eira moved between the stove and the counter as she had countless times before. The familiar sight gave him a sense of comfort he had not felt in days.","This was how home was supposed to feel.","The doorbell rang.","Ethan Yates stood in the hallway with a box from a local bakery.","\"Figured I shouldn’t show up empty-handed.\"","Alpha Sebastian let him in.","From the living room, Ethan could see Eira preparing dinner while Sebastian relaxed on the couch.","The scene looked surprisingly normal.","[He had thought the separation was settled. Had Sebastian changed his mind?","And if he had, where did that leave Serena?]","Ethan pushed the questions aside.","[Until the divorce was final, Eira was still the Luna of Hale Pack. Whatever was happening between her and Sebastian was none of his business.]","In the kitchen, Eira’s phone buzzed on the counter.","[I’m outside.]","Eira wiped her hands and left the kitchen.","\"Lila’s here. I’ll get the door.\"","She opened it just as the bell rang again.","Lila stood in the hallway, holding up a bottle of wine with a proud grin.","\"I borrowed one of Killian’s favorite bottles.\"","Eira raised an eyebrow.","\"Fine,\" Lila admitted. \"He doesn’t know I borrowed it.\"","\"Come in.\"","Lila looked down at her shoes. \"Shoes off?\"","\"Yes. You can wear these.\"","Eira handed her a new pair of slippers.","Lila’s eyes widened. \"Did you buy these for me?\"","\"I picked them up while I was out. They looked about your size.\"","\"Then I’m keeping them.\"","\"That’s why I bought them.\"","Lila smiled as she changed her shoes. \"You bought me a gift. We’re officially best friends now.\"","\"They’re slippers, Lila.\"","\"They still count.\"","Eira could not help smiling.","Lila stepped inside. Her smile cooled when she noticed the two men in the living room.","\"Alpha Sebastian. Mr. Yates.\"","Ethan immediately stood.","\"Miss Sterling. Good to see you again.\"","The Yates family was well connected, but the Sterlings operated on another level. Even Ethan knew when to be on his best behavior.","Lila gave him a polite nod, set the wine on the counter, and followed Eira into the kitchen.","Once the door closed behind them, Ethan looked at Alpha Sebastian. \"When did Eira become friends with Lila Sterling?\"","\"I don’t know.\"","\"You don’t know?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression tightened. \"I said I don’t know.\"","Ethan leaned back.","He had seen Eira and Lila talking at the charity gala, but that could have been simple courtesy. A private dinner was different.","The two women were clearly close.","Alpha Sebastian stared at the closed kitchen door.","He had been married to Eira for four years, yet someone else had become one of her closest friends without him even noticing.","--","In the kitchen, Eira glanced at Lila.","\"It gets hot in here. You can wait in the living room if you want. I probably won’t be much fun while I’m cooking.\"","\"That’s why I’m staying.\" Lila rolled up her sleeves. \"I’d be a disaster near the stove, but I can hand you things and keep you company. Just tell me what to do.\"","Eira pointed to a stack of plates. \"You can set the table.\"","\"Perfect. That’s almost impossible to mess up.\"","Lila picked up the plates and continued talking.","\"My dad cooks for my mom sometimes. Mom can barely make toast, but she always stays in the kitchen with him. She hands him things and tells him he’s doing an amazing job.\"","Eira smiled as she chopped the vegetables. \"Does he like that?\"","\"He loves it. It’s embarrassing.\"","Lila carried the plates to the counter, then came back for the silverware.","\"I asked Mom why she bothered standing there when Dad did all the work. She said being bad at something doesn’t mean you leave the other person to handle it alone.\"","Her voice softened.","\"I guess that goes for family, relationships, and friends.\"","Eira thought of Luna Seraphina. She was warm, thoughtful, and deeply loved by her family.","\"You have a wonderful mother.\"","Lila looked at her. \"You must have had someone like that too.\"","\"What makes you say that?\"","\"Because someone taught you how to care about people.\"","Eira’s hands slowed.","\"Miss Gwen did. Professor Thorne too.\"","\"Then I already like them.\"","With Lila setting the table and keeping her company, dinner came together faster than Eira expected. For the first time in years, cooking did not feel like another duty waiting to be finished.","Lila took one bite of the fish and lit up. \"This is incredible.\"","She tried the vegetables next. \"Okay, this might be even better.\"","Ethan laughed. \"We get it, Miss Sterling. You like the food.\"","\"What am I supposed to do, play it cool?\" She took another bite. \"Someone spent hours cooking for us. The least we can do is say thank you.\"","\"Fair enough.\" Ethan raised his glass. \"Dinner’s great, Eira. Thank you.\"","\"You’re welcome.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. \"She always handles dinner.\"","Lila turned to him. \"And that means you can’t thank her?\"","\"It’s how we divide things at home.\"","\"Great. Then you can handle the dishes tonight.\"","Alpha Sebastian stared at her. \"Why would I do that?\"","\"Because she cooked. That’s how teamwork works.\"","Ethan pointed to the bakery box on the counter. \"For the record, I brought dessert.\"","Lila nodded in approval. \"Smart man. You’re off the hook.\"","Then she looked back at Alpha Sebastian. \"What did you bring to the table?\"","\"This is my home.\"","\"That wasn’t the question.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression tightened.","He looked at Eira, clearly waiting for her to step in. In the past, she would have changed the subject or found some way to defend him.","Tonight, she simply placed another piece of fish on Lila’s plate.","\"Try this one.\"","\"Thanks.\" Lila smiled at her before reaching for the wine. \"Speaking of things I brought, I raided Killian’s private collection.\"","Ethan checked the label and nearly choked.","\"You took this from Alpha Killian Sterling?\"","\"Borrowed,\" Lila corrected. \"He has plenty.\"","She poured the wine, then pulled out her phone.","\"Mind if I take a picture? I need to rub this in my brother’s face.\"","\"Go ahead.\"","Lila snapped a photo of the table and sent it to Alpha Killian.","[You’re stuck on a business trip. I’m eating Eira’s cooking and drinking your wine. Try not to cry about it.]","A reply appeared almost at once. [You took my wine?]","Lila grinned but did not answer. Let him stew for a while.","A moment later, Eira’s phone lit up.","[Miss Crawford, I just landed and learned that you scheduled a client meeting before I can even check into the hotel. We need to have a conversation about your definition of \"efficient.\"]","Eira replied without hesitation. [You asked for the shortest possible trip. You’re welcome.]","A moment later, Alpha Killian answered. [I expect a written apology when I get back.]","[Request denied.]","Lila leaned over and caught her brother’s name on the screen.","\"Is Killian giving you a hard time again?\"","Alpha Sebastian looked up sharply.","\"Again?\"","Lila waved a hand. \"He likes giving her grief. It’s practically his favorite hobby.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression darkened. \"You and Alpha Killian text each other often?\""]},{"number":63,"title":"Chapter 63 She Lost Out","paragraphs":["\"No. It’s just work.\" Eira placed her phone facedown on the table. \"This is my first time working as an executive assistant. If I make a mistake, Alpha Killian tells me.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. She sounded too quick to defend him.","Alpha Killian was known for being cold and demanding. Alpha Sebastian did not believe he was simply giving Eira helpful advice.","\"You were never cut out for office work,\" he said. \"You’re better at taking care of a home. Even Lila agrees that you’re a good cook.\"","Lila slowly lowered her fork.","\"That is not what I said.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked at her.","\"I said Eira’s cooking was good. You somehow heard that she should quit her job and stay home.\" Lila gave him a cool smile. \"That’s quite a leap. Do you misunderstand people this badly at work too?\"","Alpha Sebastian forced a polite expression. He had no interest in starting a fight with Alpha Killian Sterling’s sister.","\"You misunderstood me, Lila.\"","\"No. You put words in my mouth.\"","She turned to Eira.","\"Are you really leaving Sterling Group?\"","\"In about two weeks.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s mood improved at once. He placed a piece of fish on Eira’s plate.","Eira looked down at it but did not touch it.","Lila noticed there was nothing spicy on the table.","\"Wait. Which dish is your favorite?\"","Eira paused. \"I didn’t make one.\"","\"Why not?\"","\"Sebastian has a sensitive stomach,\" Ethan explained. \"He doesn’t eat spicy food.\"","Alpha Sebastian nodded. \"I prefer simple food.\"","Lila stared at him.","\"So Eira has been eating whatever you like for four years, and you say that like it’s perfectly normal?\"","\"It’s only dinner,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","\"Every night for four years is not only dinner.\"","Lila reached for her wine.","She had been taking small sips throughout the meal. Now she finished the rest of her glass and poured a little more.","Eira gave her a warning look. \"Slow down.\"","\"I’m fine.\"","Lila took another drink. A few minutes later, her cheeks were pink and her eyes had gone slightly unfocused.","Ethan watched her sway toward Eira.","\"Is she seriously drunk already?\"","\"She doesn’t handle alcohol well,\" Eira said.","Lila rested her head on Eira’s shoulder and wrapped both arms around her.","\"Eira,\" she mumbled. \"Don’t leave me here.\"","Eira understood the signal.","\"Lila’s had too much to drink. I’ll take her home.\"","Alpha Sebastian stood. \"Call her family’s driver.\"","\"My phone’s dead,\" Lila mumbled. \"And don’t call my parents. They’ll give me a whole lecture.\"","She lifted one finger to her lips, lost her balance, and nearly slipped from the chair.","Eira caught her.","\"All right. I’ll take you back to your apartment.\"","\"Thank you,\" Lila whispered, leaning against her.","Her sudden sweetness reminded Eira of the younger children at the group home. They often held on to her the same way when it was time for her to leave.","Eira smiled and gently moved a strand of hair from Lila’s face.","Alpha Sebastian stared at her.","For one brief moment, he imagined her holding a child of their own with that same tenderness.","The thought caught him off guard.","\"You can ask Alpha Killian to pick her up,\" he said.","\"He’s out of state.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression changed. \"How do you know?\"","Eira gave him a flat look.","\"I arranged his trip.\"","Alpha Sebastian realized how unreasonable the question had sounded, but the tension in his face remained.","\"I’ll drive you.\"","\"No,\" Lila said at once. Her drunken voice was suddenly firm. \"I don’t want you coming.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s jaw tightened.","Eira helped Lila stand, then looked at Ethan.","\"I’m sorry to leave while you’re still here.\"","Ethan waved her off. \"Don’t worry about me. I can get myself home.\"","\"I’ll take her,\" Eira said to Alpha Sebastian. \"You two can finish dinner.\"","\"Come back when you’re done,\" Alpha Sebastian said as he opened the door. \"I’ll wait up.\"","Eira acted as if she had not heard him.","She had no intention of coming back.","--","As soon as the door closed, Ethan turned to Alpha Sebastian.","\"Okay, what is going on with you?\"","Alpha Sebastian returned to the table. \"What are you talking about?\"","\"You got jealous over a text from her boss.\"","\"I wasn’t jealous.\"","\"Sure.\"","Ethan leaned back in his chair.","\"You offered to drive her. Now you’re waiting up for her.\"","\"She’s my wife,\" Alpha Sebastian said. \"Of course I’m responsible for her.\"","Ethan studied him.","\"You’ve spent years chasing Serena, but now that Eira is actually leaving, you won’t let her go. Are you sure this is only about responsibility?\"","Alpha Sebastian did not answer.","His gaze fell on Eira’s place setting. Half her rice remained, and she had not touched the fish he had placed on her plate.","She used to eat anything he gave her without complaint.","Tonight, she had barely eaten.","--","Lila’s driver was already waiting downstairs.","\"Miss Sterling. Miss Crawford,\" he said, opening the back door for them.","Lila pulled Eira into the back seat and climbed in after her.","\"Go, go, go,\" she urged. \"Before Alpha Sebastian comes after us.\"","The driver pulled away from the apartment building.","Once they were a few blocks away, Lila dropped the drunken act and sat up with a grin. She was tipsy, but nowhere near as drunk as she had pretended to be.","\"How was that? Pretty convincing, right?\"","\"You nearly fell out of your chair.\"","\"I was committed to the role.\"","Eira smiled. \"Thank you.\"","\"Anytime. I just wish we could’ve finished dinner. I tried everything, so I don’t feel too bad, but you barely ate.\"","\"I wasn’t very hungry.\"","\"That’s not an answer.\" Lila pulled out her phone. \"We’re ordering food when we get to my place. Something spicy this time.\"","\"Can you still eat?\"","\"A little. But this is mostly for you.\"","She opened a delivery app, tapped the wrong button twice, then handed the phone to Eira.","\"You do it. My fingers aren’t cooperating.\"","\"The wine is catching up with you.\"","\"I said I wasn’t that drunk. I never said I was sober.\"","Eira ordered Buffalo wings and loaded fries, choosing a hotter sauce for herself and a milder one for Lila."]},{"number":64,"title":"Chapter 64 When Are You Coming Back?","paragraphs":["By the time they reached Lila’s apartment, the food was already on its way.","As they stepped inside, Lila’s phone buzzed.","A message from Alpha Killian filled the screen.","You raided my wine collection? We’ll talk when I get home.","Lila stared at the message, then grabbed Eira’s arm and gave her a pleading look.","\"You’ll have my back when Killian comes after me over that bottle, right?\"","\"I’ll tell him it was partly my fault.\"","\"I don’t mean just tonight. I mean from now on.\"","\"Of course,\" Eira said. \"You’re my friend.\"","Lila brightened. \"And Killian?\"","\"My boss.\"","\"That’s it?\"","\"What else would he be?\"","\"You’re no fun.\" Lila kicked off her shoes. \"Forget him. Tonight is girls’ night.\"","The food arrived soon after. They sat on the rug around the coffee table with Buffalo wings, loaded fries, and Coke.","Lila tried a mild wing and frowned.","\"This barely counts as hot.\"","\"You’ve been drinking. I wasn’t taking any chances.\"","\"I can handle spice.\"","\"You couldn’t handle your phone in the car.\"","\"The screen kept moving.\"","\"The car was moving.\"","Lila paused. \"Okay, fair. Next time, we’re getting the hot wings.\"","Eira laughed and handed her the ranch.","She thought of the care packages from Miss Gwen and the children.","\"Miss Gwen sent me some treats from back home. I’ll bring you a few tomorrow.\"","\"What kind?\"","\"Spicy peanut brittle, cookies, dried fruit.\"","Lila’s eyes lit up. \"Bring everything.\"","\"I said a few.\"","\"We’re best friends. Best friends don’t hold out on snacks.\"","\"You declared us best friends over a pair of slippers.\"","\"And now you’re feeding me. This friendship just keeps getting better.\"","Eira shook her head, smiling.","Her phone lit up on the coffee table.","Sebastian: [When are you coming back?]","She turned it facedown without replying.","Lila noticed but didn’t ask. She kept the conversation light and never pushed Eira to talk about anything she wasn’t ready to share.","--","Back at the Hale apartment, Alpha Sebastian checked his phone again.","Eira’s only reply had been:[I can’t leave yet.]","Alpha Sebastian sat on the couch, checking his phone while the remains of dinner grew cold on the table.","Ethan stood and grabbed his coat. \"She’s probably staying at Lila’s. Want me to stick around?\"","\"No. Go home.\"","Once outside, Ethan texted Serena.","[Sebastian’s in a mood. You might want to check on him before it starts affecting the bid. He’s at home.]","Serena almost ignored the message.","After their argument at Eden Garden, Alpha Sebastian had sent her an expensive handbag instead of offering a real apology.","Still, she could not afford to give Eira an opening.","Twenty minutes later, she rang Alpha Sebastian’s doorbell.","He opened it almost at once. \"Why didn’t you use the code?\"","Then he saw Serena, and his expression changed. He had been expecting Eira.","Serena noticed but pretended not to. \"I don’t have the code.\"","\"Right.\"","Alpha Sebastian stepped aside. Serena entered and glanced at the four place settings on the table.","\"Looks like I missed dinner.\"","\"Ethan, Lila, and Eira were here.\"","\"Where’s Eira?\"","\"She took Lila home.\"","The irritation in his voice told Serena everything.","\"You’re waiting for her.\"","\"I’m not.\"","\"Then why did you look so disappointed when you opened the door?\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression hardened. \"Drop it, Serena.\"","She flinched, and he immediately regretted his tone. \"Sorry. I shouldn’t have snapped.\"","Serena forced a small smile and wrapped her arms around him.","\"I missed you.\"","Alpha Sebastian did not return the embrace. His gaze moved to the front door again.","Serena’s arms tightened. He was still waiting for Eira.","She quickly changed the subject.","\"Sebastian, I have access to data from the Sovereign Processor Initiative. Do you need it? I’m looking forward to celebrating your success.\"","---","The next morning, Eira woke early out of habit.","She made breakfast for Lila, left her a note, and packed an extra serving for Kate before heading to Sterling Group headquarters.","Alpha Killian was still away on business, with Miles and Natalie traveling with him. That left Eira and Kate alone in the executive office.","Eira placed a container on Kate’s desk.","\"I made extra.\"","Kate opened it and found a breakfast sandwich, crispy potatoes, and fresh fruit.","\"You made all this?\"","\"I hope you like it.\"","Kate took a picture before digging in.","[My coworker fed me. I’m never leaving this job.]","Less than a minute later, a notification appeared.","Killian Sterling liked your post.","Kate nearly dropped her fork.","Alpha Killian had never liked one of her posts before.","Eira noticed her staring at the screen. \"Everything okay?\"","\"Yep. Totally normal.\"","Kate quickly put down her phone and took a bite.","\"This is ridiculously good.\"","Eira smiled. \"I’m glad.\"","By lunch, Eira had stopped by the Hale apartment while Alpha Sebastian was at work. She picked up a few personal items and some treats from Miss Gwen’s care packages, then brought them back to the office.","The smell of chili soon caught Kate’s attention.","\"What do you have under there?\"","Eira pulled a bag of chili-lime kettle chips and a container of spicy peanut brittle from beneath her desk.","\"Treats from back home. Want some?\"","\"Is that even a question?\"","Kate tried a chip and immediately reached for another.","\"These are dangerously addictive.\"","\"Too spicy?\"","\"My mouth is on fire, but I regret nothing.\"","She snapped another picture.","Fed twice in one day. I’ve officially been spoiled.","Alpha Killian liked that post too.","Comments from Miles and Natalie followed almost at once.","Miles: Save some for us.","Natalie: We leave for one trip and Kate gets all the good stuff?","Kate laughed and opened a delivery app.","\"Coffee and dessert are on me. What do you want?\"","\"You don’t have to.\"","\"I know. Now pick something before I order for you.\"","Eira gave in. \"Iced tea.\"","\"Done.\"","By the end of the day, Eira had divided the remaining treats into a few smaller bags.","When she left the building, a blush-pink Ferrari was waiting at the curb.","\"Eira!\"","Lila leaned across the passenger seat and waved.","Several employees near the entrance turned to look. Rumors were already flying about the former administrative employee Alpha Killian had suddenly promoted. Seeing Lila Sterling pick her up gave the office gossips something new to talk about.","Eira walked over with two reusable totes.","\"Trying to make a scene?\"","Lila glanced at the car. \"Hey, blame the Ferrari.\"","She pushed open the passenger door.","\"Thanks for breakfast. I was with my mentor this morning, or I would’ve driven you to work too.\"","\"You didn’t have to pick me up.\"","\"I know. That’s what friends do.\"","Eira got in and fastened her seat belt.","Lila pointed at her. \"Don’t look so nervous. I’m a great driver, no matter what Killian says.\"","\"He told me to hold on for dear life.\"","\"That jerk.\"","Eira laughed as Lila pulled away from the curb.","\"We’re going to the Thorne residence, right?\" Lila asked.","\"Yes. I need to tell Beatrice and Denny that I’m moving out.\"","Until her own house was ready, Eira planned to stay in Professor Davies’s guest room.","When they reached the Thorne residence, Denny welcomed Lila inside.","Eira set the totes on the table and handed Lila a small bag of treats.","\"Try these. If you like them, I’ll bring you more.\"","Lila hugged the bag to her chest. \"Best day ever.\"","\"They’re snacks.\"","\"Snacks you gave me. Big difference.\"","She took a few pictures and sent them straight to Alpha Killian.","Eira made me breakfast.","She gave me snacks too.","You get nothing.","Several states away, Alpha Killian read the messages between meetings.","Kate had already posted Eira’s breakfast and snacks. Now Lila was rubbing both in his face while he worked through the schedule Eira had packed with back-to-back meetings.","He typed a reply.","[Enjoy it while it lasts.]","Lila grinned at the screen.","Before she could answer, Eira’s phone began to ring."]},{"number":65,"title":"Chapter 65 You’re Avoiding Me","paragraphs":["It was Alpha Killian.","\"Alpha Killian.\"","Lila immediately leaned closer.","\"You seem to have plenty of time to feed everyone while I’m stuck with the schedule from hell,\" Alpha Killian said.","Lila rolled her eyes. \"Someone’s jealous.\"","Alpha Killian heard her. \"Lila.\"","\"What?\" she called toward the phone. \"Not my fault you missed out.\"","\"I can freeze your research budget with one call.\"","Lila sat up straight. \"Wow. No need to go nuclear. I’ll save you some.\"","\"Keep them.\"","Eira hid a smile.","\"I’ll set aside snacks for Miles and Natalie too,\" she said.","\"Good.\"","Alpha Killian hung up.","Eira looked at Lila. \"Is he always this cranky?\"","\"Most days he barely talks. Trust me, silence is his best feature.\"","Beatrice laughed from across the room.","\"Stay for dinner, Lila.\"","\"Gladly.\"","They had just sat down when Eira’s phone rang again.","This time, it was Alpha Sebastian.","\"Are you still at work?\" he asked.","\"No. I’m at Beatrice’s.\"","\"I’m outside Sterling Group.\"","Eira paused. \"Why?\"","\"I came to pick you up.\"","In four years, Alpha Sebastian had never once picked her up from work. Now that their marriage was ending, he had suddenly decided to try.","\"You knew I was staying with Beatrice.\"","\"I thought you might be at the office.\"","Beatrice held out her hand. Eira passed her the phone.","\"Sebastian,\" she said.","\"Mrs. Thorne.\"","\"I’m keeping Eira with me for a while. The house has been too quiet since my husband passed, and I could use the company.\"","\"Of course,\" he said. \"Whatever you need.\"","\"I knew you’d understand. \"She returned the phone to Eira.","\"Come home when you can,\" Alpha Sebastian said quietly.","His concern had come years too late. \"And don’t forget your weekend class. It’s close to the apartment.\"","\"I remember. We’re about to eat, so I have to go.\"","\"Eira, wait. I wanted to...\"","She ended the call.","Outside Sterling Group, Sebastian lowered his phone and stared at the dark office windows.","He had driven there on impulse, expecting to take Eira home.","Instead, she had barely given him a minute.","For years, she had waited for whatever time he chose to give her.","Now she would not even stay on the phone.","---","At dinner, Beatrice looked across the table at Eira.","\"So the settlement is signed. You’re just waiting for the judge to make it final?\"","\"Yes. The final order should come through in a little over two weeks.\"","Once the court issued it, Eira would still have to update her status within the werewolf community. That part, however, could not be discussed in front of Beatrice.","Lila kept eating, but her attention was clearly on the conversation.","\"Do you think Sebastian might try to drag it out?\" Beatrice asked.","Eira hesitated. \"Roger put the Hale family attorney in charge of the filing. He has plenty of connections in town.\"","That was what worried her. He could make sure everything stayed on track, or find a way to delay it.","\"Would he really pull something like that?\" Beatrice asked.","\"I doubt it. The Hales have wanted Sebastian to marry Serena for years. They think the Winthrop name and her family connections make her a better match.\"","Beatrice snorted.","\"Give me a break. Serena has been riding her grandfather’s name her entire career. Connections can open doors, but they can’t do the work for her.\"","\"Exactly,\" Lila said around a bite of food.","Beatrice pointed her fork at Eira.","\"And don’t let Sebastian sweet-talk you into staying. Four years is a long time, but it’s no reason to waste a fifth.\"","\"I know.\"","Eira gave a small smile, but it did not reach her eyes.","\"I wanted someone who was all in. I thought Sebastian was.\"","\"You were wrong about him,\" Beatrice said gently. \"That doesn’t mean you were wrong to want more.\"","Eira lowered her gaze.","Beatrice pushed a serving dish toward her.","\"Now eat before Lila cleans us out.\"","Lila looked up. \"Hey, I left plenty.\"","\"You’re on your third helping.\"","\"It’s really good.\"","Eira could not help smiling.","--","After dinner, Eira walked Lila to the door.","\"Text me when you get home.\"","\"Will do.\"","Lila placed the bag of treats carefully on the passenger seat of her blush-pink Ferrari.","Eira paused.","The Hales had always tossed Miss Gwen’s packages into the trunk as if they were junk taking up space. Lila handled the same kind of gift as if it mattered.","Because it had come from Eira, it mattered to her.","\"Good night,\" Eira said.","\"Night. And thanks again.\"","Lila drove back to the Sterling Manor, humming along with the radio.","She found Luna Seraphina stretched out on the couch with a sheet mask on her face.","\"You’re in a good mood,\" Luna Seraphina said.","\"I had dinner with Eira and Mrs. Thorne.\" Lila held up the bag. \"Eira gave me treats from the children’s home too. That’s how you know we’re real friends. You don’t share food from back home with just anybody.\"","\"Let me see.\"","Luna Seraphina held out her hand, but Lila pulled the bag closer.","\"Hold on.\"","Luna Seraphina looked at her. \"What?\"","\"They came from the children’s home where Eira grew up. You’re not going to be weird about that, are you?\"","Luna Seraphina slowly sat up.","\"Why would I be?\"","\"Some people think homemade food from places like that is cheap or dirty.\"","\"Those people are idiots,\" Luna Seraphina said. \"Homemade care packages beat overpriced gift baskets any day. Now hand it over.\"","Lila relaxed.","\"I knew you’d get it.\"","\"You clearly didn’t, or we wouldn’t be having this conversation.\"","\"Fair enough.\"","Lila pulled out a container of chili peanut brittle.","\"This is Eira’s favorite. Her cooking is amazing, so I’m betting this is good too.\"","She broke off two pieces and handed one to her mother.","The brittle tasted sweet and nutty at first. A second later, the chili kicked in.","Seraphina’s eyes widened.","\"That has some serious heat.\"","Lila reached for another piece. \"But it’s good.\"","\"I didn’t say it wasn’t.\"","They kept eating.","By the time Alpha Julian came home, the container was almost empty. Luna Seraphina and Lila sat on the couch with flushed cheeks, red lips, and water glasses in their hands.","Alpha Julian stopped in the doorway.","\"What happened in here?\"","\"Nothing,\" Lila said.","Luna Seraphina reached for the last piece.","Lila grabbed it first.","\"Hey. I called it.\"","\"You did not.\"","\"I was thinking it.\"","\"That doesn’t count.\"","Alpha Julian looked from them to the empty container.","\"I’m not even going to ask.\"","\"Good call,\" Luna Seraphina said.","Lila snapped a picture and sent it to Eira.","[Mom and I finished the whole container. No regrets.]","Eira replied with a voice message.","\"You ate all of it? Drink some water. And if your stomach starts fighting back tomorrow, don’t say I didn’t warn you.\"","Lila laughed and played the message for her mother.","Eira smiled at the photo, then forwarded it to Miss Gwen.","Everyone loved the care package. My friends finished the peanut brittle in one night. Please tell the kids it was a huge hit.","Before she could put away her phone, another message appeared.","Sebastian:[ Did you stop by the apartment today?]","A second message followed.","[If you can come back during the day, why won’t you stay here at night?]","Then a third.","[You’re avoiding me.]"]},{"number":66,"title":"Chapter 66 Phase One, Complete","paragraphs":["Eira’s heart skipped.","The last thing she needed was Alpha Sebastian realizing that she had been quietly moving the divorce forward.","To him, Eira was the safe choice. She kept his home running and made his life easy. Serena was the woman he wanted.","As long as Alpha Sebastian believed he could have both, he would never willingly let Eira go.","Time was running out. Once the Sovereign Processor Initiative launched, the value of Eira’s patents could rise overnight. If the divorce was delayed, Alpha Sebastian might try to claim that part of the research had been developed during their marriage. Even if he did not win, the dispute could tie up her patents and future royalties for years.","Alpha Sebastian spent three hundred thousand dollars a month on another woman but gave Eira three thousand to run their home.","Why should he get anywhere near the money from her work?","She replied at once.","[No.]","Then she added:","[I stopped by during lunch to pick up the care packages from the children’s home. Beatrice and my friends like the treats. Your family doesn’t, so I didn’t leave any behind.]","Alpha Sebastian felt a stab of guilt.","[My parents and Isabella just aren’t used to that kind of food. They didn’t mean to hurt you.]","[It’s fine.]","Eira had heard that excuse enough times.","She changed the subject.","[You worked late today. Will you be at the office late tomorrow too?]","The familiar concern in her message put Alpha Sebastian at ease.","[Yeah.]","[I’ll bring you dinner tomorrow.]","Alpha Sebastian smiled.","[I’ll forgive you for disappearing this week, but you owe me dinner twice a week from now on.]","Eira stared at the message.","Even now, he treated her cooking as something he was entitled to.","She typed one word.","[Okay.]","Then she searched for a private chef.","Alpha Sebastian knew the taste of her cooking. Over the years, Eira had adjusted every dish to suit him, down to the amount of salt, sugar, and seasoning.","Fortunately, she had written everything down.","She opened a file titled Alpha Sebastian’s Food Preferences and sent the dinner notes to a local chef who offered private meal delivery.","[Please follow the measurements exactly and pack everything in insulated containers.]","The chef confirmed the order.","That took care of Alpha Sebastian.","Eira opened her messages with Isabella.","When are you giving my box back?]","Isabella did not reply for half an hour.","Then a message appeared.","[Tomorrow night. Ten o’clock. The Sterling House]","Eira frowned.","Why would Isabella ask her to meet at a hotel?","--","At five the next evening, the private chef let Eira know Alpha Sebastian’s dinner was ready.","She booked a courier, and the insulated containers reached his office half an hour later.","Alpha Sebastian soon texted her. [Tastes just like yours. Perfect. Thanks, babe.]","Eira stared at the last word, then locked her phone.","At nine thirty, Eira checked the location Isabella had sent. The address led to Sterling House, the flagship hotel of Sterling Hospitality.","When Eira entered the lobby, Mrs. Black, the general manager of Sterling House, came over to greet her.","\"Good evening, Miss Crawford.\"","Eira was surprised. \"You remember me?\"","\"Of course. Mr. Sterling personally asked us to take care of you during your last visit.\" Mrs. Black smiled. \"I also heard you’re his new executive assistant.\"","News traveled fast within Sterling Group.","\"I’m off the clock tonight,\" Eira said. \"I’m just meeting someone.\"","\"Understood. If you need anything, let me know.\"","Mrs. Black gave her a business card and returned to the front desk.","Eira texted Isabella. [I’m here. Where are you?]","[Ninety-ninth floor. Observatory Lounge.]","Another message followed.","[You’re probably not on the guest list. Don’t worry. I’ll get you in.]","Eira ignored the smug tone.","Mrs. Black arranged elevator access before Isabella could even call downstairs.","The Observatory Lounge occupied the top floor of Sterling House. It had a restaurant, a wine bar, and several private seating areas for VIP guests.","Isabella was waiting in a corner booth. A cardboard box sat beside her feet, while half-eaten appetizers and two glasses of white wine covered the table.","She gave Eira a lazy wave. \"Sit.\"","Eira went straight for the box.","Isabella planted one heel on top of it, denting the cardboard.","Eira’s expression cooled. \"Get your foot off my box.\"","\"Easy. It’s not going anywhere.\"","Eira sat across from her. \"What do you want?\"","Isabella admired her diamond-covered nails. \"Like them? Serena paid for them. She’s a lot more generous than you ever were.\"","\"They’re nice.\"","\"That’s it?\"","\"I came for the box, Isabella.\"","\"You’ll get it when I’m ready.\"","She pushed a plate of cold fries toward Eira. \"I ordered too much. Finish them.\"","\"You brought me here to eat your leftovers?\"","\"Call it the price of admission.\"","Eira looked at the box under Isabella’s heel. \"Is everything still inside?\"","\"I didn’t bother checking.\"","\"Then give it back.\"","\"Not yet.\" Isabella tapped the box with her shoe. \"Play nice, and we’ll be done in no time.\"","Eira knew Isabella was enjoying this. Arguing would only give her another excuse to damage the children’s letters and drawings.","She finished the few fries left on the plate. \"There. Now give me the box.\"","Isabella pointed to the untouched glass of wine. \"Not so fast. Drink that too.\"","Eira looked at the glass. \"Why?\"","\"Because I’ve never seen you drunk.\"","\"I don’t drink much.\"","\"No kidding. Every holiday, the rest of us had fun while you sat there acting like a saint.\"","\"Someone had to drive.\"","Isabella laughed.","\"That’s not what Sebastian said. He told Mom and Dad you couldn’t drink because somebody had to clean up after dinner. Even the housekeeper got the holidays off. You didn’t.\"","Eira’s gaze hardened.","Isabella slid the wine closer. \"Bottoms up. Finish it, and the box is yours.\"","She finally moved the package onto the sofa beside her. The lid had already been opened. Eira could see the children’s letters, drawings, and handmade gifts inside.","They appeared to be intact.","\"You’ll hand it over after one drink?\"","\"Cross my heart.\"","\"Your word isn’t worth much.\"","Isabella’s smile tightened. \"Then call the cops if I break it.\"","\"You stole a package addressed to me. I could call them now.\"","\"Go for it. Sebastian will get me a lawyer and make it disappear. He always cleans up my messes.\"","Her confidence was not entirely fake. Alpha Sebastian had protected her from consequences before.","Eira looked at the open box.","The children had made those gifts by hand. If Isabella lost her temper, she could destroy them in seconds.","\"One glass,\" Eira said. \"Then I get the box.\"","\"That’s the deal.\"","Eira picked up the wine.","Isabella watched every move she made.","That should have set off alarm bells, but her hand was already resting on the box.","Eira raised the glass and drank.","Isabella’s smile spread as the last drop disappeared.","Phase one was done."]},{"number":67,"title":"Chapter 67 Ice and Fire","paragraphs":["\"You held up your end of the deal.\" Isabella nodded at the box. \"It’s all yours.\"","Eira stood, but the room shifted under her feet.","One glass of wine should not have hit her this hard.","She picked up the box and held it tightly against her chest.","Behind her, Isabella texted Serena.","[Done.]","[You didn’t make her drink it right away, did you?]","[No. I made her eat first, just like you said. She finished the whole glass.]","[Good. My guy’s on his way up. Get her into the room and get out.]","Isabella slipped her phone into her purse and followed Eira toward the elevator.","Eira’s vision blurred. She missed the elevator button twice before steadying herself against the wall.","Isabella laughed. \"One glass took you out? That’s just sad.\"","Eira’s legs were weak, and heat was spreading through her body.","This was not alcohol.","She turned to Isabella. \"What did you put in my drink?\"","For a second, panic flashed across Isabella’s face.","Then she rolled her eyes. \"Nothing. You’re just a lightweight.\"","\"Give me my phone.\"","\"You have it.\"","Eira reached into her purse and found both her phone and Mrs. Black’s business card. Her fingers shook as she entered the number.","Isabella saw the card and lunged for her.","\"Who are you calling?\"","Eira had just entered the last digit when Isabella ripped the phone from her hand.","\"You’re drunk. Quit making a scene.\"","Isabella shoved the phone into her purse before Eira could place the call.","Eira tried to grab it back, but her knees gave out. She dropped to the carpet and curled around the box.","\"Give it back.\"","\"I’m trying to help you.\" Isabella raised her voice for the hallway cameras. \"Come on. Let’s get you to bed.\"","She hauled Eira up and dragged her into the elevator.","Eira bit the inside of her cheek, fighting to stay conscious. She could barely stand, but she refused to let go of the box.","Isabella took her down a quiet private hallway and stopped outside a room near the end.","\"I told you to slow down,\" she said loudly. \"You never listen.\"","She swiped the key card and pushed Eira inside.","Eira fell to her knees.","\"Help,\" she whispered.","Isabella shut the door. By then, Eira’s grip had weakened enough for her to pull the box away.","She snapped a picture and sent it to Serena.","[She passed out. Is that supposed to happen?]","[Did you give her too much?]","[No. I did exactly what you told me. She’s burning up.]","[Then stick to the plan. Get out now.]","Isabella looked down at Eira.","For the first time that night, she felt a flicker of fear.","Then she grabbed her purse and left, checking the door behind her to make sure it had locked.","A man was walking down the hall as she headed for the elevator.","He passed her without a word and continued toward Eira’s room.","Isabella stepped into the elevator. As the doors closed, a grin spread across her face.","Step two was done.","---","Inside the room, Eira heard the lock click behind Isabella.","She forced her eyes open. Her vision blurred, and her legs could barely hold her weight. Cold sweat covered her skin, yet her body burned from the inside.","This was no ordinary alcohol.","She did not have time to figure out Isabella’s plan. She had to stay awake.","Eira bit hard into the skin between her thumb and forefinger. Pain cut through the fog, giving her a few seconds of clarity.","She stumbled toward the bathroom, hitting the wall twice before reaching it. Once inside, she locked the door and turned the shower as cold as it would go.","The icy water hit her fully clothed body.","She shivered, but the heat did not fade.","Still, the cold kept her conscious.","For now, that was enough.","--","A black Maybach pulled up outside Sterling House.","Alpha Killian stepped out with Miles and another assistant. He looked exhausted. Eira had packed a week of meetings into three days, leaving him barely enough time to sleep.","Mrs. Black, the hotel’s general manager, came downstairs to welcome him.","At the same moment, Isabella crossed the lobby on her way out.","She froze when she recognized Alpha Killian.","After the way he and Lila had embarrassed her at Eden Garden, seeing him was the last thing she wanted. She quickly turned away and headed for the doors.","\"Welcome back, Mr. Sterling,\" Mrs. Black said. \"We weren’t expecting you until tomorrow.\"","Alpha Killian loosened his tie. \"Neither was I. You can thank Miss Crawford and her schedule.\"","\"Miss Crawford is here tonight, actually.\"","Alpha Killian stopped.","\"She’s here again?\"","The last time Eira had come to Sterling House, she had arrived with a handprint on her face and tears in her eyes.","\"Is something wrong?\" he asked.","\"Not that I know of,\" Mrs. Black said. \"She came to meet someone in the Observatory Lounge.\"","Alpha Killian’s concern eased, replaced by annoyance.","\"Good to know she’s having a night out while I work the schedule from hell.\"","Mrs. Black hid a smile.","Alpha Killian turned to Miles. \"Call her. I want an update on everything that happened while I was gone.\"","Miles paused. \"You said no one was to bother you tonight.\"","\"I changed my mind.\"","Miles reached for his phone, but Alpha Killian held out his hand.","\"You’re taking too long. Give me that.\"","He called Eira himself.","A ringtone began to play across the lobby.","Alpha Killian looked toward the sound.","Near the entrance, Isabella stopped dead.","The ringing was coming from inside her purse."]},{"number":68,"title":"Chapter 68 Breaking Down Doors","paragraphs":["The ringtone came from inside Isabella’s purse.","Her mind went blank.","She fumbled with the clasp, but before she could silence the phone, a shadow fell over her.","Alpha Killian stood behind her.","His expression was cold enough to make her blood run colder. \"Why do you have Eira’s phone?\"","\"I don’t know what you mean.\"","\"Try again.\" His voice stayed low, but the Alpha command beneath it hit Isabella like a physical force. Her knees almost gave out.","Tears filled her eyes as she pulled out the phone. \"She was drunk. She must’ve dropped it into my purse.\"","Alpha Killian took the phone from her.","He did not believe a word. Fear poured off Isabella in waves, and beneath the sharp smell of her perfume, his wolf caught the bitter scent of a lie. \"Where is she?\"","\"She passed out.\"","\"What room?\"","\"I don’t remember.\" Alpha Killian stepped closer. His Alpha pressure filled the space between them.","Isabella stumbled back.","\"You’re lying,\" he said.","Mrs. Black immediately turned to the security desk. \"I’ll check the cameras and key card records.\"","\"Do it,\" Alpha Killian ordered.","He looked at Miles. \"Don’t let Miss Hale leave.\"","Miles moved in front of the exit.","Isabella’s face went pale. \"You can’t hold me here.\"","\"Want to bet?\" Miles asked.","A few minutes later, Mrs. Black returned.","\"Room 9908. Miss Hale took her there about fifteen minutes ago.\"","Alpha Killian headed straight for the private elevator, with Natalie and Mrs. Black close behind.","When they reached Room 9908, they found the door unlocked.","Alpha Killian pushed it open.","Cold water ran over his shoes. A cardboard box covered in children’s drawings sat near the wall, and water streamed from beneath the bathroom door.","Alpha Killian caught Eira’s scent beneath the smell of wine and chemicals.","\"Eira!\"","Something fell inside, but she did not answer.","Natalie spotted the box. \"That’s hers. It came from the children’s home.\"","Alpha Killian tried the bathroom door.","Locked.","He pounded on it. \"Eira, move away from the door.\"","Silence.","Natalie went pale. Her wolf hearing caught a heartbeat on the other side, weak and uneven.","\"Alpha, her heartbeat is fading.\"","Alpha Killian’s eyes flashed gold.","\"Back up.\"","He kicked beside the lock. The frame cracked, and the door flew open.","Water rushed into the bedroom.","Eira lay fully dressed in the bathtub. Her body covered the drain while the faucet continued to run. Her face was bright red, but her lips had turned pale. The water was almost high enough to cover her nose.","Alpha Killian crossed the bathroom, shut off the faucet, and pulled her from the tub. Heat poured through her soaked clothes.","\"What the hell did they give you?\"","Eira dug her nails into his arm.","\"No,\" she whispered. \"Please...\"","Her eyes were open, but she did not recognize him.","\"It’s me.\" Alpha Killian softened his voice. \"You’re safe, Eira.\"","She kept struggling, weak but terrified.","Natalie crouched beside them.","\"Eira, it’s Natalie. Alpha Killian and I are here to help.\"","Eira slowly turned toward her.","\"Na... talie?\"","\"Yes. I’m right here.\"","Alpha Killian caught the chemical scent rising from Eira’s skin. His jaw tightened.","\"This isn’t alcohol. She was drugged.\"","He lifted her into his arms.","\"Call Dr. Wood.\"","Natalie pulled out her phone.","Barry Wood was the youngest high-ranking wolf physician in the Sterling Pack. He specialized in treating werewolf reactions to human drugs, silver exposure, and forced heat suppressants. He was also Alpha Killian’s private doctor, which meant he could be trusted to keep Eira’s condition away from human hospital records.","\"Dr. Wood,\" Natalie said as soon as he answered. \"We need you at Sterling House right now.\"","Alpha Killian lifted Eira into his arms.","\"Tell him to bring a full toxicology kit.\"","Natalie repeated the order.","\"Where should he meet us?\" she asked.","\"My suite,\" Alpha Killian said. \"Now.\"","He carried Eira out of the flooded bathroom.","Her fingers remained locked around his arm.","Even half-conscious, she was still terrified someone would take her away.","---","Meanwhile, Isabella paced across the lobby.","A few minutes earlier, the man Serena had hired had stormed out of the hotel with soaked pants and a furious look on his face.","Something had gone very wrong.","Isabella wanted to warn Serena, but Miles had not taken his eyes off her. Two hotel security guards were also waiting near the exits.","Miles watched her make another turn around the seating area.","\"You’re wearing a hole in the floor, Miss Hale.\"","\"I need to go home.\"","\"Not yet.\"","\"You can’t keep me here.\"","\"Hotel security can ask you to stay while they investigate a possible crime against a guest,\" Miles said calmly. \"You’re also free to call an attorney.\"","Isabella tightened her grip on her phone. \"I didn’t do anything.\"","\"Then you have nothing to worry about.\"","\"Easy for you to say.\"","Miles gave her a cool smile. \"You’re the one with Eira’s phone in your purse.\"","Isabella had no answer.","She should never have chosen Sterling House. Serena had offered to cover the bill, and Isabella had wanted the best hotel in the city. Now they were trapped inside Alpha Killian Sterling’s territory.","The lobby doors opened.","Alpha Sebastian and Serena walked in.","Relief rushed over Isabella. \"Sebastian!\"","Serena saw Miles and immediately knew the plan had fallen apart.","The man she had hired had already called her. He claimed Eira had locked herself in the bathroom and flooded the room before he could touch her. He had fled when he heard people coming.","Serena had told Alpha Sebastian only part of the story.","Someone had seen Eira enter Sterling House and go upstairs with a man.","Isabella rushed over and pulled Serena aside.","\"Alpha Killian found Eira,\" she whispered. \"Your guy ran, and Miles won’t let me leave.\"","Serena’s eyes narrowed. \"Eira is with Alpha Killian?\"","Isabella nodded.","A new plan formed in Serena’s mind.","Alpha Killian was far more useful than the man she had hired. If Alpha Sebastian found Eira in Alpha Killian’s private suite, he would assume the worst.","Serena raised her voice just enough for Alpha Sebastian to hear.","\"Isabella, are you sure you saw Eira go upstairs with another man?\"","Isabella caught on.","\"Positive.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s face hardened. \"What room?\"","\"I don’t know. I came downstairs, and Miles stopped me.\" She pointed toward him.","Miles’s expression cooled.","Alpha Sebastian strode toward him.","\"Where is my wife?\"","\"And where is Alpha Killian?\""]},{"number":69,"title":"Chapter 69 I’ll Stay","paragraphs":["Presidential Suite","Eira lay on the bed, wrapped in a robe and a thick blanket. Natalie had taken off her wet coat and shoes, but her clothes were still damp.","Without the cold water, the heat inside her came roaring back.","She twisted under the blanket and clawed at her collar.","\"Easy.\"","Alpha Killian caught her wrists before she could hurt herself.","Eira looked up at him. Her eyes were unfocused, and her breathing came in short, uneven bursts.","She fought him again.","Alpha Killian used his tie to bind her wrists loosely together.","\"Tell Wood to step on it.\"","\"He’s on his way up,\" Natalie said.","Eira pulled against the tie and let out a weak sound. Alpha Killian leaned closer to check the knot, and her warm breath brushed his face.","Her scent hit him a second later.","His wolf surged forward.","Alpha Killian backed away at once.","\"Natalie, stay with her.\"","He stepped onto the balcony and let the cold air clear his head. His clothes were still soaked, but he barely noticed.","All he could think about was Eira lying in that bathtub, seconds from drowning.","The doorbell rang.","Dr. Barry Wood stood outside with his medical bag.","\"You look like hell,\" Barry said.","\"It’s not me. Get inside.\"","Barry entered the bedroom and stopped when he saw Eira.","Then he noticed Alpha Killian’s red tie around her wrists.","\"I’m guessing there’s an explanation.\"","\"She was scratching herself,\" Alpha Killian said. \"Help her.\"","Barry got to work.","He checked her pulse and pupils, then drew a blood sample. His expression quickly turned serious.","\"She was drugged. Her heart rate is way too high.\"","\"Can you treat it?\" Alpha Killian asked.","\"Not until I know what she took. If I give her the wrong medication, I could make it worse.\"","Natalie frowned. \"Can’t her wolf burn it out?\"","\"She doesn’t have one,\" Alpha Killian said.","Barry looked up sharply. \"She’s wolf-less?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"That’s a problem. A werewolf’s system can regulate most human drugs. Hers can’t.\"","Eira struggled again. Her pulse climbed on the monitor.","\"What about another cold bath?\" Natalie asked.","\"No chance,\" Barry said. \"Her body temperature is already too low. Ice water could put her into shock.\"","Alpha Killian’s patience snapped.","\"Then give me an option that actually helps.\"","Barry thought for a moment.","\"My grandmother may recognize the reaction. She’s a licensed acupuncturist and one of the oldest healers in the pack. She’s handled cases like this before.\"","\"Call her.\"","\"She doesn’t make house calls anymore.\"","\"Then we’ll go to her.\"","Barry nodded. \"Her clinic is twenty minutes away.\"","\"Tell her we’ll be there in ten.\"","Alpha Killian returned to the bed and untied Eira’s wrists. He wrapped the blanket securely around her and lifted her into his arms.","She grabbed the front of his shirt.","\"Don’t,\" she whispered. \"Please don’t leave me.\"","Alpha Killian went still.","\"I’m not going anywhere.\"","Barry stared at him.","\"So this is Miss Crawford.\"","\"Don’t even go there,\" Alpha Killian warned.","Barry raised both hands. \"Didn’t say a word.\"","Natalie quickly texted Miles.","We’re taking Eira to Dr. Wood’s family clinic. Keep Isabella in the lobby and do not share our location.","They headed for the private elevator.","As the doors closed, Sebastian, Serena, and Isabella stepped into another elevator across the lobby.","One car went down while the other went up.","They missed each other by seconds.","---","Even wrapped up like a burrito, Eira would not stay still.","She shifted restlessly in Alpha Killian’s arms, weak sounds slipping from her lips.","Each movement made the blanket slide against his chest, bringing her soft curves closer despite his effort to keep a safe distance.","\"Easy,\" Alpha Killian murmured. His voice came out lower and rougher than he intended.","He touched her cheek, hoping to calm her.","The second her hot skin met his palm, heat shot up his arm.","She turned instinctively into his touch, rubbing her flushed cheek against his hand as if searching for relief. Her lips brushed the base of his thumb, warm and slightly parted.","His wolf stirred.","Alpha Killian pulled his hand back and tightened his grip on the blanket instead.","His fingers dug into the thick fabric. It was the only thing between his hands and her heated skin, and suddenly it did not feel thick enough.","Eira opened her eyes. Her gaze was hazy, but it locked on him.","Her lashes fluttered. Then her eyes dropped slowly to his mouth.","For a moment, Alpha Killian forgot to breathe.","Every instinct demanded that he pull her closer, shield her with his body, and soothe the ache twisting through her.","He shut those instincts down hard.","Then she struggled again, and he caught her before she could slide from his lap.","\"Hold still,\" he said through clenched teeth. \"We’re almost there.\"","Eira made a small sound and pressed closer. Her breath slipped beneath the open collar of his shirt, hot against his throat.","Alpha Killian’s jaw tightened.","\"You smell good,\" she whispered.","The words were slurred and barely clear, but he heard every syllable.","His entire body went rigid.","Natalie sat beside him, pretending not to notice how stiff his entire body had become.","In the passenger seat, Barry glanced at the rearview mirror.","Alpha Killian was holding Eira as if she might break. He did not dare pull her closer, but he would not loosen his grip either.","Barry’s mouth twitched.","Alpha Killian caught his eye in the mirror.","\"Something funny?\"","\"Nope.\"","\"Then face forward.\"","Barry wisely looked away and called his grandmother.","--","Twenty minutes later, they reached the Wood family clinic.","Mrs. Wood was waiting in a private treatment room. She was one of the Sterling Pack’s oldest healers and a licensed acupuncturist who had spent decades treating wolves whose bodies reacted badly to human medicine.","A deep wooden soaking tub stood in the center of the room. Steam rose from water scented with medicinal herbs.","She took one look at Eira.","\"Put her on the table first.\"","Alpha Killian carried Eira inside and gently set her down.","Mrs. Wood checked Eira’s pulse, lifted one eyelid, and smelled her breath.","\"Strong stimulant mixed with something meant to lower her judgment,\" she said. \"Her body is fighting it, but without a wolf, she has no way to control the reaction.\"","\"Can you help her?\" Alpha Killian asked.","\"I can bring down her heart rate and help her system clear the drug.\"","She opened a leather case filled with sterile needles, then nodded toward the door.","\"Barry, wait outside.\"","Barry blinked. \"You don’t need me?\"","\"I need someone she trusts and someone strong enough to keep her from slipping under the water.\"","Natalie stepped forward. \"I can stay.\"","The older woman looked at Eira, who was still clutching Alpha Killian’s shirt.","\"She isn’t holding on to you.\"","Natalie followed her gaze.","Eira’s fingers were locked around the front of Alpha Killian’s shirt, even in her dazed state.","Alpha Killian nodded once.","\"I’ll stay.\""]},{"number":70,"title":"Chapter 70 The Wood Family Clinic","paragraphs":["Before leaving, Natalie paused at the door.","\"What should we do downstairs? Alpha Hale knows Eira is at the hotel.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression turned cold.","\"His sister set this up. Save every second of security footage, pull the key card records, and call the police. No one leaves until we know exactly what happened.\"","\"What about Alpha Hale?\"","\"Keep him away from Eira. If he causes trouble, have security escort him out.\"","\"Got it.\"","Natalie closed the door behind her.","Mrs. Wood turned back to the tub.","\"Her wet clothes need to come off. I’ll cut them away and keep her covered. You hold her shoulders and make sure she doesn’t move when I place the needles.\"","Alpha Killian’s jaw tightened. \"Shouldn’t Natalie stay instead?\"","\"She can’t hold Eira steady if she starts fighting again,\" the older woman said. \"I need your strength, and your scent is keeping her calmer.\"","Alpha Killian looked at Eira. Sweat covered her flushed face despite the warm herbal bath, and her breathing remained fast and uneven.","He crouched beside the tub but kept his hands to himself.","\"Eira, listen to me.\"","Her eyes opened slowly.","\"Your wet clothes have to be removed so she can treat you,\" he said. \"She’ll do it, not me. I only need to hold you still. Do you understand?\"","Eira struggled to focus on him, then gave a faint nod.","\"I may have to touch your shoulders and back,\" Alpha Killian added. \"Is that okay?\"","She nodded again.","A tear slipped down her cheek.","Alpha Killian caught it with his thumb before he could stop himself.","\"You’re safe,\" he said quietly. \"No one here is going to hurt you.\"","Mrs. Wood placed a folded towel across Eira’s chest and gave Alpha Killian a sharp look.","\"Eyes up, Alpha.\"","His gaze immediately returned to Eira’s face.","\"I know.\"","\"Good. Hold her steady.\"","Alpha Killian slid one arm behind Eira’s shoulders, keeping the towel firmly in place while the older woman carefully cut away the soaked fabric beneath the water.","Eira flinched and grabbed his wrist.","\"I’ve got you,\" Alpha Killian said. \"Just hold on.\"","--","Sterling House","Mrs. Black allowed Alpha Sebastian to inspect Room 9908 with hotel security present. Serena and Isabella followed him upstairs.","Water covered the hallway. Inside the room, staff were running wet vacuums, and the bathroom door hung from its broken frame.","Isabella stopped cold.","\"What the hell happened?\"","Alpha Sebastian turned on her. \"You booked this room?\"","\"I was helping Eira. She had too much to drink, so I brought her up here.\"","\"You left her alone in this mess?\"","\"Alpha Killian came looking for her,\" Isabella said quickly. \"He must’ve taken her.\"","Serena picked up the story at once.","\"Doesn’t Alpha Killian keep a private suite here?\"","Mrs. Black’s expression cooled. \"Alpha Killian’s whereabouts are private.\"","\"Then call him,\" Isabella snapped. \"He took Eira’s phone from me.\"","Mrs. Black held her gaze.","\"Why did you have Miss Crawford’s phone?\"","Isabella had no answer.","Alpha Sebastian looked around the flooded room, his patience gone.","\"My wife is missing, the bathroom door has been kicked in, and no one will tell me what happened. Call Alpha Killian, or I’m calling the police.\"","\"The police have already been contacted,\" Mrs. Black said. \"We’re treating this as a possible crime scene.\"","Alpha Sebastian pulled out his phone and called Eira again.","This time, she answered.","\"Eira?\"","\"It’s me,\" she whispered.","Her weak voice wiped the anger from his face.","\"Where are you? Are you hurt?\"","He heard an older woman speaking in the background.","\"The Wood Family Clinic,\" Eira repeated faintly. \"You can look it up.\"","The call ended.","Alpha Sebastian headed for the elevators.","Serena hurried after him. \"You found her?\"","\"She’s at a clinic.\"","\"Is Alpha Killian with her?\"","Alpha Sebastian did not answer.","Back in the lobby, Miles blocked Isabella before she could follow.","\"Not you, Miss Hale.\"","She glared at him. \"Get out of my way.\"","\"Security footage shows you handling Eira’s wineglass. An on-site test also found an unknown substance in the leftover wine.\"","The color drained from Isabella’s face.","\"That’s crazy. I didn’t put anything in her drink.\"","Miles raised an eyebrow.","\"I never said you did.\"","Isabella realized her mistake too late.","\"You’re trying to pin this on me.\"","\"No one is pinning anything on you. The police are on their way, and you’re going to answer their questions.\"","She turned to Alpha Sebastian.","\"You’re really leaving me here?\"","Alpha Sebastian hesitated, but Serena took his arm.","\"Eira may be in trouble. We need to go.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked at Miles. \"Make sure my sister is treated fairly.\"","\"She’ll be treated exactly as the evidence requires,\" Miles said.","\"Sebastian!\" Isabella called after him.","He left with Serena.","The moment they got into the car, Serena texted Isabella.","[Keep your cool. Don’t admit to anything. Alpha Sebastian always has your back. He’ll fix this.]","A second message followed.","[I’m going with him to find out what happened. Once Eira is gone and Sebastian and I are together, I’ll help you study abroad. You know I take care of family.]","Isabella read the messages twice.","Her panic eased. Alpha Sebastian had always bailed her out before, and Serena had too much to lose to abandon her now.","She sat on a lobby sofa and crossed her legs.","\"Fine. I’ll answer their questions.\"","Then she waved toward the front desk.","\"Fine. I’ll cooperate. But if you’re keeping me here, the least you can do is get me a coffee.\"","--","Alpha Sebastian and Serena arrived at the Wood Family Acupuncture Clinic minutes later.","The moment they entered, they spotted Natalie and Dr. Wood in the waiting room.","Serena’s eyes flickered. That settled it. Alpha Killian was here with Eira.","She slipped her arm through Alpha Sebastian’s and said softly, \"Looks like Alpha Killian brought her here himself.\"","Then she gave a small, knowing smile.","\"Must be nice to have a boss who makes house calls.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression turned cold."]},{"number":71,"title":"Chapter 71 The Lawsuit Against Isabella","paragraphs":["Barry caught the bite beneath her friendly tone.","\"Alpha Sebastian and I go way back,\" Serena said. Her eyes swept through the clinic, searching for Eira and Alpha Killian. \"But I’ve never seen a boss drop everything for an employee before.\"","Natalie’s smile held.","\"Then I guess tonight’s full of firsts.\"","Serena ignored the jab.","\"Where are they?\"","Alpha Sebastian was already looking down the hall.","Eira heard their voices from the treatment room.","\"I’m here,\" she tried to call, but her throat was too dry.","Mrs. Wood opened the door.","\"She’s in here.\"","Alpha Sebastian stepped inside.","Eira was resting in a carved wooden chair, dressed in a loose linen top and matching pants provided by the clinic. Her damp hair fell around her pale face.","Alpha Killian stood beside her, holding out a cup of warm water.","Their fingers brushed as Eira took it.","Alpha Sebastian stopped.","The quiet scene hit him harder than it should have. Alpha Killian stood close to Eira as if that was exactly where he belonged.","Alpha Sebastian crossed the room and put himself between them.","Alpha Killian looked at him with open contempt.","\"Nice of you to finally show up, Alpha Hale. Another minute in that bathtub, and your wife might not be alive.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked at Eira. \"What happened?\"","Eira took a sip of water before answering.","\"Isabella stole a care package that belonged to me. She said I could get it back if I met her at Sterling House.\"","Serena’s fingers tightened around her purse.","\"She made me drink a glass of wine. It was drugged. Then she took my phone and left me in a hotel room. A man came in, so I locked myself in the bathroom and used cold water to stay awake.\"","Sebastian’s face went pale.","\"Alpha Killian and his staff found me in the tub,\" Eira finished.","\"You think Isabella planned all that?\" Alpha Sebastian asked. \"She screws up, but this is way over the line. Maybe she didn’t know the wine was drugged.\"","Alpha Killian gave a cold laugh.","Serena lowered her eyes, hiding her satisfaction.","Eira looked at Alpha Sebastian without emotion.","\"I’m not asking what you think.\"","He froze.","\"I know what happened to me,\" she continued. \"I’m filing a police report, and I’m pressing charges.\"","\"Eira, hold on. We don’t have all the facts.\"","\"You don’t. I do.\"","Alpha Killian stepped forward.","\"Sterling House has the security footage, key card logs, wineglass, and test results. The police will get all of it.\"","He met Sebastian’s stare.","\"Your sister isn’t walking away from this one.\"","\"Is that a threat?\" Alpha Sebastian asked.","\"It’s a reality check.\"","Alpha Killian turned to leave.","In the hall, he handed Eira’s phone to Barry.","\"Don’t let Hale take her anywhere until your grandmother clears her.\"","Barry glanced toward the treatment room.","\"He’s her husband?\"","\"For now.\"","Barry raised his eyebrows. \"That’s a hell of a mess.\"","Alpha Killian gave him a warning look.","Barry lifted both hands. \"I’ve got it. She stays.\"","Alpha Killian left with Natalie.","--","When Barry returned, Alpha Sebastian was still making excuses for his sister.","\"This could be a misunderstanding.\"","\"Exactly,\" Serena said. \"Bella can be spoiled, but she’d never plan something like this.\"","Eira looked straight at her.","\"You’re half right. Isabella is mean enough to do it. She’s just not smart enough to come up with the plan.\"","Serena’s smile tightened. \"What’s that supposed to mean?\"","\"If Isabella had planned it, she would’ve shoved the wine at me the second I sat down. Instead, she showed off her diamond manicure, made me eat her leftovers, and offered me the drink last.\"","It had all felt normal because Isabella had humiliated Eira for years. The first two demands had made the third seem like more of the same.","Someone had understood Isabella’s habits and used them to lower Eira’s guard.","Serena crossed her arms. \"Are you trying to blame me now?\"","\"I didn’t say your name.\"","\"You didn’t have to.\"","Eira held her gaze. \"Interesting.\"","Serena’s expression flickered.","\"If you’re going to accuse me of something, bring proof,\" she said.","\"Who says I don’t have any?\"","It was a bluff, but Serena did not know that.","\"Then let’s see it.\"","\"Knock it off,\" Alpha Sebastian said. He turned to Eira. \"I’ll talk to Isabella and get the truth.\"","\"You mean you’ll give her time to get her story straight.\"","\"That’s not what I said.\"","\"It’s what you always do.\"","Alpha Sebastian fell silent. Then he reached for her hand.","\"You’re freezing.\"","Eira pulled away. \"Then don’t touch me.\"","He caught her hand again. \"How did they treat you?\"","\"An herbal soak and acupuncture.\"","Sebastian’s eyes moved over her loose clinic clothes.","\"And before that? Alpha Killian brought you here. Did he touch you?\"","Eira stared at him.","She had been drugged, locked in a hotel room, and nearly drowned. Yet Sebastian’s first real concern was whether another man had put his hands on her.","\"He saved my life,\" she said. \"And he treated me with respect.\"","Alpha Sebastian gave a bitter laugh.","\"Alpha Killian Sterling doesn’t do anything without an angle. He’s cold, ruthless, and always three steps ahead. Don’t confuse that with being a good guy.\"","\"At least he showed up when I needed help.\"","The words landed hard.","Sebastian’s grip tightened around her hand.","\"Do you even remember who your husband is?\"","Alpha Sebastian grabbed Eira by the shoulders. His fingers dug in hard enough to make her wince.","His wolf pushed forward with his anger, sending a wave of Alpha pressure through the treatment room.","Eira felt the air grow heavy, but without a wolf, she did not react the way an Omega normally would.","\"What do you think you’re doing?\"","Mrs. Wood entered with a bowl of herbal medicine. She struck his arm with her cane.","\"Hands off my patient.\"","Alpha Sebastian released Eira.","Mrs. Wood stepped between them. She had treated three generations of wolves in the Sterling Pack.","Rank carried weight almost everywhere else, but not in her treatment room.","\"She was drugged, nearly drowned, and just went through a painful treatment,\" she snapped. \"A healthy wolf might have burned through most of that drug by now. She doesn’t have one to help her.\"","Her eyes narrowed.","\"You show up and start manhandling her instead of asking if she’s okay?\""]},{"number":72,"title":"Chapter 72 Isabella Gets Arrested","paragraphs":["Anger flashed across Alpha Sebastian’s face, but Mrs. Wood did not back down.","\"Alpha Killian showed her more care tonight than you have. He brought her water, found her towels, and listened when I told him what she needed.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s face darkened at Alpha Killian’s name.","Mrs. Wood pointed her cane toward the door.","\"If you can’t put your jealousy aside for five minutes, you can wait outside.\"","\"She’s still in pain?\" Alpha Sebastian asked.","\"I already told you I had acupuncture,\" Eira said.","Barry took the bowl from his grandmother and handed it to Eira.","\"Give her some room,\" he told Alpha Sebastian and Serena. \"You’re crowding her.\"","\"Thank you, Dr. Wood. Thank you, Mrs. Wood.\"","\"Drink up, sweetheart,\" Mrs. Wood said. \"It’s bitter, but it should help. I would’ve added honey if we’d had more time.\"","\"It’s okay.\"","Eira managed a tired smile and slowly finished the medicine.","Mrs. Wood’s expression softened. During the treatment, Eira had gripped the side of the tub and endured every needle without complaint. She had been through enough for one night.","Alpha Sebastian stepped forward.","\"Thank you for helping her. I’ll take her home now.\"","\"No,\" Barry said.","Alpha Sebastian looked at him. \"Excuse me?\"","\"She needs to stay overnight for observation.\"","Mrs. Wood caught Barry’s meaning and nodded.","\"That’s right. Her heart rate still isn’t stable, and we don’t know how long the drug will remain in her system.\"","\"I can watch her at home,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","Mrs. Wood gave him a flat look.","\"You had your chance to look after her. She stays.\"","Barry opened the door.","\"We’re a small private clinic, so we don’t have room for visitors. You can check on her tomorrow.\"","Mrs. Wood turned to Eira.","\"You can stay in my room tonight. Think you can put up with an old lady?\"","Eira nodded. \"Thank you.\"","\"Good. That’s settled.\"","Mrs. Wood offered her an arm. Eira stood, but her knees nearly gave out.","Alpha Sebastian reached for her.","Before he could touch her, Eira caught the back of the chair and steadied herself.","His hand stopped in midair.","Serena saw the instinctive concern on his face and tightened her grip on her purse.","The plan had blown up in her face. Instead of catching Eira with another man, Alpha Sebastian had found her hurt and surrounded by people who blamed his sister.","\"We should go,\" Serena said quickly. \"We can pick Eira up tomorrow.\"","\"Don’t bother,\" Eira said. \"I have work.\"","Alpha Sebastian frowned. \"You’re going to work after all this?\"","\"I’ll decide in the morning.\"","\"Or do you already have plans with someone?\"","Eira was too exhausted to take the bait.","Alpha Sebastian’s frustration flared.","\"So now you’re giving me the silent treatment?\"","He grabbed her wrist.","Eira looked down at his hand, then at Serena’s satisfied smile.","\"When did you become like this?\" Alpha Sebastian demanded.","Eira raised her eyes to his.","\"When did you start noticing?\"","Before Alpha Sebastian could answer, his phone rang.","\"It’s Bella,\" Serena said.","He answered, and his expression changed almost at once.","\"I’m coming.\"","Alpha Sebastian hung up and turned to Eira. \"I have to go. Stay put. I’ll pick you up tomorrow.\"","\"Don’t bother.\"","He ignored her. \"Let’s go, Serena.\"","She followed him out.","Once they were gone, Barry locked the clinic door and handed Eira her phone. \"Alpha Killian told me to give this back.\"","Eira looked at the screen. \"So that’s how he found me.\"","Barry hesitated. \"Alpha Sebastian isn’t your ex yet, is he?\"","\"Not officially.\"","\"And Serena?\"","Eira’s gaze dropped. \"She’s the woman he loves.\"","Barry had already connected the dots. The whole thing was a train wreck, but it was none of his business.","\"Thanks for letting me stay,\" Eira said.","\"Thank Alpha Killian. He told me not to let Hale take you anywhere.\"","Barry checked the time.","\"It’s two in the morning. Get some sleep.\"","He sent Alpha Killian a quick update.","[Alpha Sebastian’s gone. Eira is staying here tonight. She’s safe.]","Across town, Alpha Killian read the message and finally breathed easier.","A text from Eira appeared next.","[Thank you for saving me tonight, Alpha Killian. Dinner’s on me next time.]","[Fine.]","[Get some sleep.]","A low-battery warning flashed across Alpha Killian’s screen.","[I have your suitcase.]","[Please keep it safe. It means a lot to me.]","Before he could answer, his phone died.","Eira waited a few minutes, then set her phone aside. Exhaustion took over, and she fell asleep.","--","When Alpha Sebastian returned to Sterling House, Isabella was sitting on the lobby floor in the middle of a full-blown meltdown. Two police officers stood nearby while several guests watched from a distance.","\"I already told you, I didn’t do anything!\" she cried. \"You can’t haul me downtown over some made-up story.\"","\"We have a formal complaint, hotel footage, and physical evidence,\" the lead officer said. \"You need to come with us and answer some questions.\"","\"I’m not going anywhere until my brother gets here.\"","She had been stalling the whole time.","The moment she spotted Alpha Sebastian, she jumped up and ran to him.","\"Sebastian! They’re trying to pin this on me.\"","Alpha Sebastian stepped between her and the officers.","\"There must be some misunderstanding.\"","\"That’s what the investigation will determine, Mr. Hale,\" the officer said. \"Sterling House reported a suspected drugging on its property. Miss Crawford also gave a statement accusing your sister of taking her phone and leaving her in a room where another man later entered.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s expression tightened.","\"My sister says she had nothing to do with it.\"","\"And she’ll have a chance to explain that at the station. If she wants an attorney present, she can call one.\"","The officer nodded to his partner.","\"Let’s go.\"","When the second officer reached for her, Isabella grabbed Alpha Sebastian’s sleeve.","\"No. I’m not going with them.\" Her voice rose. \"Eira made this whole thing up. She’s trying to ruin me!\"","\"Bella, calm down,\" Alpha Sebastian said.","\"Make them stop. You always fix things for me.\"","The officers pulled her hands behind her and placed her in handcuffs.","\"Sebastian!\" Isabella screamed as they led her outside. \"Call the family lawyer. I’m suing Eira for defamation!\"","Alpha Sebastian watched them put his sister into the back of a patrol car.","Serena moved to his side, wearing a worried expression.","\"I can’t believe Eira let it go this far,\" she said softly.","\"The hotel called the police,\" Alpha Sebastian replied.","\"At Alpha Killian’s order,\" Serena reminded him. \"And Eira filed her own report.\"","Alpha Sebastian said nothing.","Serena lowered her voice.","\"This isn’t only about Bella anymore. Eira is working with Alpha Killian to go after your family.\"","His jaw tightened.","Serena touched his arm.","\"Whatever happened between you and Eira, she shouldn’t be using another man to punish your sister. She knows exactly what that does to you.\"","Alpha Sebastian stared after the patrol car, his expression growing colder."]},{"number":73,"title":"Chapter 73 Divided Forces","paragraphs":["Alpha Sebastian spent the rest of the night calling attorneys and trying to keep his parents out of it.","Serena made sure he failed.","Alpha Roger and Luna Margaret arrived at the police station before dawn. By then, Isabella had cried off most of her makeup.","\"Mom! Dad!\"","She rushed into Luna Margaret’s arms.","\"How did you know?\"","\"Serena called us,\" Luna Margaret said. \"Your brother planned to keep us in the dark.\"","Isabella glanced at Serena with gratitude. No matter what happened, she would keep Serena’s name out of this.","In a private conference room, with the family attorney present, Isabella admitted that she had drugged Eira and arranged for a man to enter the hotel room.","She claimed the whole thing had been her idea.","Luna Margaret stared at her.","\"You pulled this stunt at Sterling House? Seriously?\"","\"It was the nicest hotel in town, and Serena offered to cover the room.\"","The attorney looked up sharply. \"Serena was involved?\"","\"No,\" Isabella said at once. \"She only paid for the room. She had no idea what I was planning.\"","Luna Margaret pressed a hand to her forehead.","\"You could’ve picked any hotel in the city, but you chose one owned by the Sterlings. What were you thinking?\"","Alpha Roger cut in.","\"How did you get the drug?\"","\"Cash. No receipt, no texts, no online order.\"","\"And the man?\"","\"I never contacted him directly.\"","Alpha Roger leaned closer.","\"Then listen carefully. You helped Eira into the room because she was drunk. You thought you locked the door, but apparently you didn’t. A stranger walked in, realized he had the wrong room, and left. You never hired anyone.\"","\"But I did lock the door.\"","Luna Margaret gave her a hard look.","\"No, you didn’t.\"","Isabella finally caught on.","\"Right. I must’ve left it open.\"","The attorney shut his folder.","\"Stop talking. All of you. Do not contact that man or anyone else connected to this case. That could be viewed as witness tampering.\"","Alpha Roger’s face remained calm.","\"Understood.\"","He had no intention of sitting back while his daughter took the fall.","Isabella grabbed his sleeve.","\"When can I go home?\"","\"We’ll ask for bail as soon as the court opens,\" the attorney said. \"But Sterling House has video, key card logs, and physical evidence. This won’t disappear overnight.\"","Isabella’s eyes filled with tears again.","\"I can’t stay here.\"","Alpha Roger pulled his arm free.","\"You should’ve thought of that before you drugged someone in a Sterling hotel.\"","Luna Margaret turned to him. \"What do we do now?\"","\"You talk to Eira. Get her to call it a misunderstanding and stop cooperating with the police. I’ll handle the hotel.\"","The attorney frowned.","\"She can’t simply drop a criminal case.\"","\"No,\" Alpha Roger said. \"But the case gets a lot harder without the alleged victim.\"","Luna Margaret stepped into the hallway and called Alpha Sebastian.","\"Where’s Eira?\"","His voice cooled. \"How did you find out?\"","\"That’s not important. I need to talk to her.\"","\"She’s sick. Leave her alone.\"","\"I’m only trying to clear up this mess.\"","\"No, Mom.\"","Luna Margaret’s expression hardened.","\"Your sister is sitting in a police station.\"","\"And Eira nearly drowned.\"","\"Sebastian.\"","\"Stay away from her.\"","He hung up.","Luna Margaret stared at her phone in disbelief. Her own son had just chosen Eira over his family.","She called Serena next.","\"Where is Eira?\"","Serena paused, pretending to struggle with the question.","\"Sebastian told me not to tell anyone.\"","\"I won’t throw you under the bus, sweetheart.\"","After another careful pause, Serena sighed.","\"She’s at the Wood Family Acupuncture Clinic.\"","\"Text me the address.\"","\"Of course.\"","Serena ended the call with a smile.","By sunrise, Luna Margaret was outside the clinic.","--","Eira woke at her usual time despite getting only a few hours of sleep.","She opened the window and took a deep breath. Her body still felt weak, but her mind was clear again.","She had survived because she had locked herself in the bathroom. If Alpha Killian had arrived even a minute later, she might have drowned.","Eira reached for her phone, wanting to thank him again, but the battery was dead. Her charger was still with her things, so she set it aside.","\"Morning, Miss Crawford.\"","Barry walked into the room.","\"Good morning. Where’s Mrs. Wood?\"","\"Out back drying herbs.\" He gave her a quick look. \"How do you feel?\"","\"A lot better.\"","\"Good. I’ll update Alpha Killian.\"","\"Do you have to?\"","\"I’m his personal physician. He dragged me out of bed in the middle of the night for you. Trust me, he’ll want a status report.\"","Barry turned toward the hall just as a sharp voice came from the clinic entrance.","\"Where’s Eira?\"","Luna Margaret.","She marched inside, then slowed when she noticed Barry.","\"Eira, we need to talk. Outside.\"","\"If this is about Isabella, save your breath. The answer is no.\"","\"I haven’t even asked you anything.\"","\"You came here at sunrise. I can guess.\"","Luna Margaret’s face tightened.","\"Isabella is still your sister. You and Sebastian aren’t divorced yet.\"","\"My sisters are the girls I grew up with.\"","For four years, Isabella had insulted Eira and everyone at the children’s home. Every time Eira objected, the Hales gave her the same tired excuse.","She’s young. She’s family. Let it go.","Eira was done letting things go.","Luna Margaret drew herself up. \"Like it or not, Isabella is your sister until that divorce is final.\"","Eira gave her a cold look.","\"Funny. Isabella never called me her sister. She called me an orphan.\"","\"So?\"","\"So if she and I are sisters, that would make you and Roger my parents too.\" Eira tilted her head. \"Should I ask when the two of you died?\"","Luna Margaret stared at her.","\"How dare you?\"","\"I’m only following your logic.\"","\"You watch your mouth!\"","\"Then stop calling Isabella my sister. You don’t get to treat me like an outsider for four years and suddenly call me family when your daughter needs a way out of jail.\"","Luna Margaret’s face turned red.","\"You ungrateful little brat.\"","Eira remained calm.","She had once swallowed every insult because she loved Alpha Sebastian and did not want to put him in the middle.","Not anymore.","Luna Margaret stepped closer.","\"You want that divorce finalized, don’t you?\"","Eira’s eyes narrowed.","\"Drop the complaint against Isabella and tell the police it was a misunderstanding. Otherwise, Roger will have our attorneys tie up that divorce for as long as they can.\"","Barry’s expression cooled.","Luna Margaret smiled as if she had finally found the right pressure point.","\"No Isabella, no divorce. Your choice.\""]},{"number":74,"title":"Chapter 74 Leverage","paragraphs":["Using the divorce as leverage?","Eira almost laughed.","\"You want this divorce more than I do,\" she said. \"If you want to keep me married to Sebastian, be my guest.\"","Luna Margaret’s face tightened.","\"But while I’m still his wife, I’ll start acting like one. Isabella can pay her own study-abroad bills. Sebastian isn’t required to bankroll his adult sister.\"","\"You wouldn’t dare.\"","\"Try me. Your house and health insurance are already covered. As for spending money, I’ll cancel the extra card and send you three thousand a month. That should sound familiar.\"","It was the same amount Alpha Sebastian had given Eira to run their household.","Luna Margaret went red.","Eira continued before she could interrupt.","\"Then there’s all the money Sebastian spent on Serena. The jewelry, handbags, and whatever else he bought her came out of marital assets. I can demand a full accounting and sue to recover every dollar.\"","Luna Margaret’s expression changed.","\"That would put Serena in an awkward spot, wouldn’t it?\" Eira asked. \"She’s an elite wolf from a top-tier pack. Do you really think she’ll settle for being a married man’s mistress forever? Even if she would, her family wouldn’t.\"","Serena wanted Alpha Sebastian, but only after Eira was out of the picture. A public fight over marital assets could destroy the polished image she had worked so hard to build.","\"And one more thing,\" Eira added. \"As long as I’m Luna Hale, I’ll attend every company dinner, charity gala, and pack event with my husband. I’ll make sure everyone knows exactly who Sebastian’s wife is.\"","That struck a nerve.","The Hales had always been ashamed of Eira’s childhood, her lack of family status, and the ordinary job they believed she had. The thought of presenting her to high society as Alpha Sebastian’s wife made Luna Margaret furious.","She pointed a shaking finger at Eira.","\"You’re cold-blooded.\"","\"Of course,\" Eira said. \"Serena is the sweet one.\"","Luna Margaret’s chest rose and fell.","\"So, are you still planning to hold up the divorce?\"","Of course she was not.","Luna Margaret wanted Eira out of the family as soon as possible. Unfortunately, the legal waiting period was not over, and the judge could not issue the final order for another two weeks.","\"What will it take for you to back off Isabella?\" Luna Margaret demanded. \"The police don’t have enough to convict her. Sebastian will get her out, so what are you trying to prove?\"","\"If she has nothing to worry about, why are you here?\"","Luna Margaret fell silent.","Eira knew the Hales would pull every string they could to protect Isabella. That was not the point.","Luna Margaret wanted her daughter out of the holding cell before breakfast. She wanted no criminal record, no scandal, and no consequences.","Eira wanted Isabella to face every one of them.","Luna Margaret took a breath and changed tactics.","\"Name your price. Money, a house, whatever you want. Tell the police it was a misunderstanding.\"","\"There is no misunderstanding.\"","\"Then tell me what you want.\"","Eira met her eyes.","\"Nothing you can give me.\"","---","Meanwhile, Alpha Sebastian had been waiting in the lobby of Sterling Tower since early that morning.","By noon, Alpha Killian still had not agreed to see him.","The message was loud and clear. Sterling House intended to hold Isabella responsible for the damage she had caused, including the flooded room, the police investigation, and the possible harm to a hotel guest.","Alpha Sebastian was willing to write a check. Money was not the problem.","He needed the Sterlings to back off before the case became public. If Isabella was charged, the scandal would not stop with her. It would damage the Hale name and give his business rivals plenty of ammunition.","In his world, reputation was currency.","Upstairs, Miles entered Alpha Killian’s office.","\"Alpha, Sebastian Hale is still downstairs.\"","Alpha Killian did not look up from the document in front of him.","\"Let him wait.\"","Miles hid a smile. \"Understood.\"","Alpha Killian had returned from a brutal business trip the night before, only to spend the rest of the night dealing with Eira’s emergency.","He had not slept at all.","Every time he closed his eyes, he saw her again.","Eira fighting the drug with everything she had. Eira nearly drowning in the hotel bathtub. Eira clinging to him as he carried her out.","Then came the memories he had tried much harder to forget.","Her wrists loosely bound with his red tie so she would not hurt herself. Her warm breath against his neck in the car. Her fingers gripping his shirt as she begged him not to leave.","At the clinic, she had endured the treatment without crying out. Even weak and pale afterward, she had looked at Alpha Sebastian with a quiet strength that refused to break.","Alpha Killian had taken more than one cold shower when he got home.","It had not helped.","His wolf had remained restless, furious at the people who had hurt her and far too aware of how she had felt in his arms.","Now Alpha Sebastian Hale had shown up to clean up his sister’s mess.","Alpha Killian picked up another file.","He could sit downstairs all day.","Miles left Alpha Killian’s office and found Natalie filling Kate in on the night before.","She had just reached the part where Alpha Killian kicked down the bathroom door.","\"He took it out with one kick,\" Natalie said. \"The whole frame cracked.\"","Kate stared at her, a bag of Eira’s chili-lime chips in her hand.","\"You’re kidding.\"","\"I was standing right there.\"","Natalie stole a chip. Kate pulled the bag away.","\"Hey. Eira gave these to me.\"","\"And she gave me some too. Mine are at the hotel.\"","Miles walked over, and Kate offered him the bag.","\"Want one? Just don’t clean me out.\"","He took a chip.","\"When is Eira coming back?\" Kate asked.","\"This afternoon.\"","\"That’s it? She should take a few days off.\"","\"She only has two weeks left before she resigns,\" Natalie said. \"Good luck convincing her to stay home.\"","Kate lowered her voice.","\"What’s Alpha Killian going to do when she leaves?\"","Natalie and Miles exchanged a look.","\"Pretend he doesn’t care,\" Miles said.","From inside the office, Alpha Killian’s cold voice carried into the hall.","\"Lunch.\"","Miles immediately straightened.","\"Coming, Alpha.\"","Halfway through lunch, Alpha Killian finally spoke.","\"What time is Eira coming in?\"","Miles kept his face blank.","\"She’s due back at two thirty.\"","Alpha Killian gave a short nod and continued eating as if the question meant nothing.","When they returned to the office, Miles received an update from the lobby.","\"Alpha Sebastian finally left.\"","\"Good.\"","Alpha Killian had refused to meet with him. Sterling House would not bury the incident just because Alpha Sebastian offered to cover the damage.","At two o’clock, another message arrived.","Miles read it twice before stepping into Alpha Killian’s office.","\"Alpha, Isabella Hale was released on bail.\"","Alpha Killian’s expression hardened.","\"Did Eira back down?\"","\"No. Her police report is still active.\"","\"Then how did Isabella get out?\"","Miles hesitated.","\"Sterling House withdrew its separate complaint and agreed not to oppose bail.\"","Alpha Killian slowly raised his eyes.","\"Who authorized that?\"","\"Your father.\"","The pen in Alpha Killian’s hand hit the desk with a sharp crack.","Miles remained still.","Alpha Killian picked up his phone and called his mother.","Luna Seraphina answered on the second ring.","\"If you’re looking for your father, don’t bother. He knew you’d be mad, so he’s avoiding you.\"","\"He went over my head.\"","\"He did.\"","\"You both promised to stay out of company business unless it was an emergency.\""]},{"number":75,"title":"Chapter 75 A Drumbeat Heart","paragraphs":["\"This wasn’t a business decision,\" Luna Seraphina said. \"Someone called in a serious favor, and your father decided it wasn’t worth starting a war over one spoiled Hale girl.\"","\"She drugged an employee in one of our hotels.\"","\"I know. I already tore him a new one.\"","Then Luna Seraphina’s tone changed.","\"Still, this is the first time you’ve gone this far for a woman who supposedly means nothing to you.\"","Alpha Killian said nothing.","Luna Seraphina continued.","\"I asked you a question the last time we spoke.\"","Her voice softened.","\"Do you have an answer for me now, Killian?\"","\"I have my answer.\"","Alpha Killian ended the call just as Eira walked into the executive office.","She wore an oatmeal sweater, a matching skirt, and rimless glasses. Her olive coat hung over one arm, and she carried two paper bags in the other.","She still looked a little pale, but she was steady.","When their eyes met, Alpha Killian’s heart kicked hard against his ribs.","Eira gave him a polite nod, then placed the bags on Natalie’s and Miles’s desks.","\"I kept the snacks mild. I wasn’t sure how much heat you could handle.\"","Natalie looked inside and grinned. \"You’re spoiling us.\"","\"Don’t get used to it.\"","\"No promises.\"","Miles thanked her and caught Alpha Killian watching from his office. He quickly looked away.","A moment after Eira sat down, a message appeared on her screen.","Killian: My office.","She picked up a file and went in.","\"The trip summary and follow-up schedule,\" she said, placing it on his desk.","Alpha Killian flipped through the brief, well-organized report.","\"What happened to my written apology?\"","\"Still denied.\"","The corner of his mouth twitched.","\"Worth a shot.\"","He closed the file.","\"Sterling House is issuing a formal apology and a guest-safety payment for what happened last night.\"","\"The hotel didn’t drug me.\"","\"It happened under our roof. That makes it our problem.\"","Eira started to argue, but Alpha Killian cut her off.","\"Accounting already has your direct deposit information. The payment will hit your account today. Any restitution from the Hales will be handled separately.\"","His tone made it clear the decision was final.","\"Thank you,\" Eira said.","Then she hesitated.","\"When are you free for dinner?\"","Alpha Killian looked up. \"Dinner?\"","\"I owe you one. You saved my life.\"","\"Anytime.\" The answer came a little too fast.","He leaned back and added casually, \"Just send me the details.\"","\"I will.\" Eira turned to leave.","\"Wait.\"","Eira looked back.","Alpha Killian studied her pale face. \"Go home if you start feeling sick.\"","\"I’m fine.\"","\"You nearly drowned less than twenty-four hours ago.\"","\"But I didn’t.\"","Stubborn. Completely unreasonable.","Somehow, he liked that about her too.","Eira returned to her desk and worked through the rest of the afternoon.","Shortly before five, her phone buzzed.","Wire received: $300,000.","A message from Alpha Killian followed.","[[Sterling House paid half. The Hales paid the other half through their attorney’s escrow account. Neither payment requires you to withdraw your statement or give up your legal rights.]","Eira stared at the amount. [Thank you, Alpha Killian.]","The typing bubble appeared, vanished, then returned.","A minute later, his reply came through.","[There’s something else. Sterling House settled its civil claims against the Hales for the damage to the hotel. We won’t pursue a separate lawsuit.]","He sent another message before she could respond.","[That does not affect your police report or the criminal investigation.]","So that was what he had been reluctant to tell her.","Someone with enough influence had convinced the Sterling family to settle. Alpha Killian clearly did not agree with the decision, but he had made sure it would not take away Eira’s right to keep fighting.","She typed back:[Understood.]","--","Alpha Killian stared at her one-word reply.","It felt cold. Too cold.","The message bothered him for the rest of the afternoon.","When the workday ended and Eira left without coming into his office again, he finally did something he had never done before.","He took a screenshot and sent it to Lila.","[What does this mean? Is she mad?]","Lila replied with an angry emoji, followed by a voice message.","\"Seriously? You want me to read one word with zero context? What am I, the FBI?\"","Alpha Killian did not answer.","Another message appeared.","[Also, Dad wants you home for dinner.]","[Not happening.]","[Okay, so what’s going on? Did Dad screw something up?]","[I’m busy. I need to check on something at my place.]","Eira’s soaked paintings and letters were still drying there. He wanted to see if they could be saved.","Alpha Killian grabbed his coat and headed for the garage.","His car had barely pulled onto the street when he spotted another vehicle near the curb.","Alpha Sebastian’s.","Alpha Sebastian had one hand around Eira’s wrist and was shoving her into the passenger seat. She tried to pull free, but he forced her inside and slammed the door.","Alpha Killian saw the red marks on her wrist.","His expression turned cold.","By the time his driver reached them, Alpha Sebastian’s car was already speeding away.","\"Follow them.\"","The command came out almost like a growl.","\"Yes, Alpha Killian.\"","--","Inside Alpha Sebastian’s car, Eira pulled at the door handle.","It would not open.","She turned on him. \"Did you turn on the child lock?\"","\"You wouldn’t get in the car.\"","\"So you thought kidnapping me was the next best move?\"","\"Don’t be dramatic. We need to talk.\"","\"You could’ve called.\"","\"You stopped answering me.\"","Alpha Sebastian looked exhausted. His shirt was wrinkled, and dark circles stood out beneath his eyes.","\"Isabella is out on bail,\" he said. \"Sterling House settled with us. All you have to do is tell the police you may have misunderstood what happened.\"","\"I didn’t misunderstand being drugged.\"","\"There’s no proof Isabella knew what was in that drink.\"","\"Then who put it there?\"","\"I’m trying to find out.\"","\"No, you’re trying to make the investigation go away.\"","Alpha Sebastian’s hands tightened around the steering wheel.","\"I can’t just demand Sterling House’s security footage.\"","\"The police can. That’s why my statement stays.\"","\"Do you have any idea what this could do to me?\" His voice rose. \"My wife gets drugged at a Sterling hotel, and Killian Sterling is the one who carries her out and takes her to a clinic. If that hits the press, Hale Group will be a laughingstock.\"","Eira looked out the window.","There it was. His company. His name. His pride.","Never what had happened to her.","\"If you’re that worried about bad press, maybe your sister shouldn’t have drugged me.\"","\"She made a mistake.\"","\"She set me up for an assault.\"","\"You don’t know that.\"","\"I was there, Sebastian.\"","He struck the steering wheel with his palm.","\"This affects both of us. Our company, our name, our future.\"","\"There is no our future.\"","The words came out calm and clear.","Alpha Sebastian glanced at her sharply.","\"What is that supposed to mean?\"","\"Exactly what it sounds like.\"","\"Don’t.\" His voice dropped. \"I don’t want to hear that.\"","He pulled up at a red light and grabbed her wrist.","Eira winced.","Alpha Sebastian noticed but did not release her.","\"I know you’ve had a rough couple of days,\" he said, forcing his voice to soften. \"Let me fix this.\"","Eira stared at him.","Alpha Sebastian kept going, mistaking her silence for interest.","\"You wanted the house when I asked you to quit your job, and I gave it to you. This time, you get a car. Think of it as an apology.\"","He reached toward her hair.","Eira turned away before he could touch her.","His hand stopped in midair.","It was a small movement, but it hit him hard."]}]);
